WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:16.200
FULLER: And having been a
visitor here very many times

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.890
I've had a great chance to see
life changing-- the pattern,

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:22.660
lifestyles changing
very greatly--

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.330
but the environment itself
changing tremendously.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.080
The year that I entered
Harvard, the subway

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.550
was completed and opened
from Boston to Cambridge.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:38.370
And up to this time
been really very--

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:41.450
well, MIT could get over
of Boston quite rapidly.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:45.720
But MIT-- much of it had
been in Boston in those days.

00:00:51.966 --> 00:00:56.690
Because when I was young I felt
the great change was taking

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:59.420
place that had not
been experienced

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:03.560
by my father, my
grandfather, all the family

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.010
records that I had--

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.540
I thought it might
be a good idea

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.600
to keep some record of
a little individual born

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.050
in the Victorian period
and who is coming over

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:17.030
in some kind of new world.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.760
And so I have kept
just such records.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.225
And I have really,
really large archives.

00:01:21.225 --> 00:01:24.500
And they're down in
Philadelphia right now.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.710
But by virtue of having them
I'm able to look at records,

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:32.390
they're changing things, and
get a sense of rates of change

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.780
and have some sense of
what may be unfolding

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.950
for humanity on our planet.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.930
I think it great fun.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.349
I was seven when the first
automobile came into Boston.

00:01:47.349 --> 00:01:49.390
I was eight when the Wright
brothers' first flew.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:54.830
I was brought up as inherently
impossible for man to fly.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:58.020
Those were impressionistic
years up to eight years of age.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.390
And wireless-- how
crazy can you get?

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:04.900
Even though Marconi had
invented the wireless the year

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.505
that I was born, we
don't have an SOS

00:02:06.505 --> 00:02:09.720
till I'm 12 years of age.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.911
And so these were
very extraordinary,

00:02:11.911 --> 00:02:13.910
and that was things that
were suddenly becoming,

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.309
and many things that I've
been told would never happen

00:02:16.309 --> 00:02:17.350
were beginning to happen.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.574
I was told man and never
got to the North Pole,

00:02:19.574 --> 00:02:20.740
never got to the South Pole.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.290
And when I was 14 they
did get to the North Pole.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.450
When I was 16, got
to the South Pole.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.510
So there's something
that was happening here

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.727
that all the world had
not expected that's all.

00:02:30.727 --> 00:02:32.060
That's all I'm trying to get at.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:35.470
So I felt really very
intuitive to this necessity

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:38.320
to keep some kind of
record of the transition.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.460
I'm sure it's only because I'd
did start doing that years ago

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.840
that you've invited
me to be here tonight.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.120
Because I have been
able to keep some track

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.180
and been able to make
some pregnostications

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.326
that have come true.

00:02:51.326 --> 00:02:55.630
But I don't think there's
ever been a moment our humans

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.630
on our planet--

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:01.110
by humans have really come to
know so much about our planet

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.160
and about the local
universe, where

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.090
humans have ever been in such
perilous we really are today.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:12.360
I think we're absolutely on
the brink of either doing away

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.760
with ourselves.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.210
And all of this
then relates to--

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:22.520
I wonder if it'd be possible for
me to have a chair brought out.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.821
I should have asked
for it in advance.

00:03:25.821 --> 00:03:27.090
I have podia-phobia.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.790
I don't normally get
behind these things.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:32.784
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.160
I think I'll think better
if I'm sitting down.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.257
Because I operate entirely
what I call thinking out loud.

00:03:41.257 --> 00:03:42.090
Thank you very much.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:00.700
At the age of 32 in 1927--

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.270
which is the year
that Lindbergh flew

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:05.780
across the Atlantic-- which is
suddenly a great change again,

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.440
that human beings not
only were now flying,

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.660
but they would be able
to cross great oceans.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:18.420
At the age of 32 then I decided
to really make an experiment

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.769
with the rest of my life--

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:23.740
trying to find out
what, if anything,

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:31.100
a little penniless,
unknown individual might

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:35.930
be able to do effectively
on behalf of all humanity,

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:39.830
the great nations and
great corporations

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:43.510
inherently could not do.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:47.710
So I was just fairly
simply, think about this--

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:51.700
luckily I'd been in the
regular United States Navy

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.040
and I'd had some commands.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.430
And so I could think about the
fact that 3/4 of earth is water

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:02.260
and the Navy was concerned with
that 3/4 the world is water.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:05.030
Out of the 1/4 that is
dry land, about half it

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.700
is covered with
ice, rocks, deserts.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.860
So then only about 1/8
of the surface of earth

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.610
but propitious for life support.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:19.570
And that 1/8 is invited up
into well over 100 nations,

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.500
at the time I decided
to do my experiment.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.190
So a 100 nations
dividing up 1/8--

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.580
each one of them tending
to look out for its own.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:32.650
It was so much pioneering
of humanity got it so far.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.660
She continually found herself
being attacked by others.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.490
People in America had
a little more luck

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:39.870
because they were further
away from the others.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:43.370
Anyway, quite
clearly those nations

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:46.160
were thinking about
their fraction of the 1/8

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.440
of the surface of the Earth.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:58.490
And the great corporations were
operating under the protection

00:05:58.490 --> 00:05:59.810
of the various nations.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:03.665
And they had to make profits
at a short period of time

00:06:03.665 --> 00:06:04.790
or they go out of business.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.690
At least that's the
way they thought.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:08.605
So they were inherently
shortsighted.

00:06:08.605 --> 00:06:10.490
And so there was nothing--

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.190
and nobody was thinking
about our total planet

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.950
as a ship-- a spaceship.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:21.170
Incredibly designed, and
onboard of it all these humans.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:24.890
And by this time a
radial accumulated

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:29.500
knowledge, great
identification of resources.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.720
So I said there's
nothing to stop me

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:36.190
as little individual
thinking about then,

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:37.700
this total Spaceship Earth.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:42.230
I gave it that name after a
while and it became popular.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.920
And nothing to stop
me then of seeing

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.630
about how to employ
the total knowledge

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:51.950
of the total resources to
take care of all humanity--

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:55.450
paying absolutely no attention
to any kind of divisions

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.950
of the human beings, but trying
to look at it as all humans.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:07.200
I wondered why the
universe to have humans

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.870
on board in the universe
and have them on board

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:12.270
this little particular planet.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:15.660
I found that the more
I studied human beings

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.498
in contradistinction
to other organisms,

00:07:19.498 --> 00:07:23.090
the more I was convinced we had
some very important function

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:26.550
to fulfill here in the universe.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:30.710
And the universe
had no supercargos--

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.750
that everything that
was in the universe

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.025
was essential to the
integrity of the regeneration

00:07:36.025 --> 00:07:38.250
of universe.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:42.326
So the function-- I'll come
down to it very rapidly--

00:07:42.326 --> 00:07:44.450
differentiating between
humans and other organisms.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:47.670
I said all the other
living organisms

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:52.120
have some built in integral
equipment in the organism

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:53.890
itself that gives
it special advantage

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:58.070
in some special environment,
whether kind of snout on a dog

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:00.580
to be able to dig
from the ground,

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:04.000
or some little vine that just
could grow up the Amazon--

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.815
and do it very beautifully.

00:08:05.815 --> 00:08:08.660
Or birds flying in the
sky with beautiful wings,

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:11.504
but when non-flying unable
to disencumber themselves

00:08:11.504 --> 00:08:13.170
of their wings because
they're integral,

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:16.450
if walking is a difficult
matter for the bird.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:20.380
So I said humans
then, don't have these

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:23.170
built in special equipments.

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:25.362
A lot of people identify
brain with humans,

00:08:25.362 --> 00:08:27.070
but there are many
creatures have brains.

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:30.520
And I've found that if
you want to think about it

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:33.190
in your own direct experience--

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:37.600
brains are always and only
coordinating the information

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:40.445
of the senses,
without which we are

00:08:40.445 --> 00:08:43.520
utterly unaware of universe.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.130
So they're coordinating
the special cases.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.420
This one smells a little
different than that one.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.420
So we have packages
of these special case

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:56.090
experiences which brains are
able to store and retrieve

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.150
memory of.

00:08:57.150 --> 00:09:00.220
I've found humans have a
special capability that

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:04.070
are not manifest by any other
creature, which I call minds.

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:07.890
Because I heard mind and
brain inter-exchanged,

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.550
but I'm now
differentiating clearly--

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:14.560
brains is physical equipment
for coordinating the senses.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.350
And mind-- from time to time--

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:21.200
had the capability to discover
relationships existing

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:24.050
between special
cases that were not

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:26.330
manifest by any of
the special cases,

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.690
considered only by themselves.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:31.580
As for instance, the
long extraordinary case

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.190
of human beings being
excited by the night sky,

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:40.010
all seemingly fixed eyes,
recognizable constellations.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.260
In contradistinction
to which they were one,

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:44.630
two, three from
time to time, lights

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:48.590
that appeared a little bit
brighter than the others.

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:51.060
And you could see them
moving against things,

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:53.669
but tonight they're in different
position from yesterday.

00:09:53.669 --> 00:09:55.460
So quite clearly, they
were moving around--

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:58.290
What later on we begin
to call the planets.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:01.460
And these were so
intriguing to humanity

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:03.630
that they made all
kinds of speculations.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.180
They kept records
out of them as best

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:07.310
they could in relation
to their periods

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:10.490
as seasons and
other experiences.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.680
And they gave them
names of gods.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.370
But not until human beings
have calculated capability,

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:18.850
which is really very,
very recent as far

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.350
as humanity in general goes--

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.840
which came along
with the positioning

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:27.800
of numbers and the ability
then to multiply and divide.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:30.300
If you ever tried doing your
calculations in Roman numerals,

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.080
you find how difficult it is.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:35.310
In fact, you can't
get anywhere at all.

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:39.470
So not until then these
Arabic numerals came in

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:43.010
and the cipher itself,
and they got publication

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:46.250
in northern Africa in 1200.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.080
Then it took 300
years for it to get

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:52.260
into Italy and southern
Germany, the point where

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:56.230
Copernicus, as a human being,
has calculated capability.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:58.700
And with calculating
capability and taking the data

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:01.516
regarding what we knew of these
planets and the sun in the sky

00:11:01.516 --> 00:11:03.890
was that we're one of those
planets going around the sun.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:06.110
The sun was not going around us.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:08.330
I want to really stress
how very, very recent

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:12.200
is that event
because I find today,

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:15.680
though it was 500 years
ago, we're really not--

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:18.020
and everybody knows about it--

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:24.740
we have done very little to get
ourselves actually celebrating,

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:27.135
reacting in terms of it.

00:11:27.135 --> 00:11:30.170
For instance, I
had a great honor

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:34.670
of being invited to speak
to the MIT Faculty Club

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.350
back in the early '50s.

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:42.181
And the dean of architecture
at that time was--

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:49.920
said to me that he found that
the Architecture Department was

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:53.940
never being asked to give any
Faculty Club talks because MIT

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:57.380
felt that it's so really
MIT that the Architecture

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.550
Department was sort of
a department of liaison

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:00.810
with idiots.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:02.370
[LAUGHTER]

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.080
So they were not really
taken very seriously.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:08.520
So he complained to the
other deans about it.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:12.530
And they said, all right, you'll
have the next faculty lecture.

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:15.720
And so the dean asked
me to give the talk.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:20.970
And because I knew about
his saying about the fact

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:23.620
that the family
liaison was idiots,

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:26.010
I said to the Faculty
Club when I stood up

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:28.770
I was very surprised to be asked
to speak to them because they

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:29.985
were all so ignorant.

00:12:29.985 --> 00:12:31.650
And they looked very
surprised, and I

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.040
had to make good in a hurry.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.190
[LAUGHTER]

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.950
And I said, of
any of you present

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:41.100
who do not see the sun going
down in the evening, please

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:41.977
show your hands.

00:12:41.977 --> 00:12:42.810
There were no hands.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.350
I said you've had 500 years.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:47.850
You've known the sun is not
going down for 500 years.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:49.830
What are you doing in
your educational system

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:53.070
about coordinating your
senses with your information?

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:54.900
[LAUGHTER]

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:57.280
I think it's very ignorant
to persist in this manner.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.370
Keep on saying you're
very practical to say

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:00.380
sunrise and sunset.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.360
Seems to be rather good poetry,
but you keep continually

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:06.586
standing your kids off
with misinformation.

00:13:06.586 --> 00:13:08.538
[LAUGHTER]

00:13:08.538 --> 00:13:13.600
Now, that is enough of that
particular episode, but I--

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.055
[LAUGHTER]

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:20.860
Coming back now to trying
to identify humans.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:23.560
And I said we have
this phenomena mind,

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:26.980
and we have this
matter then of planets.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:30.910
The idea suddenly that we're
one of the planets going

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.350
around the sun.

00:13:32.350 --> 00:13:34.930
And this is enormously
intrigued others.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.540
And we have Tycho Brahe
getting better instruments,

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:40.000
being a man of great means,
and making some better

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:41.030
observations.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:43.300
He needs a mathematician,
getting Kepler.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:49.360
And Kepler then discovering
that all these different planets

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:52.930
were a different distance from
the sun, all different sizes,

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.907
all going around
at different rates.

00:13:54.907 --> 00:13:56.490
So while they're all
on the same team,

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.330
seem to be very disorderly.

00:13:58.330 --> 00:13:59.950
But being a
mathematician, he said,

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:01.960
I know one thing
in common, which

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.210
is they're going around
the sun, at least that.

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:05.920
I could, as a
mathematician, give them

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.630
something else in common.

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:10.659
I might be able to find
radium with two knowns.

00:14:10.659 --> 00:14:12.450
So he said, I'm going
to give them a known.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.600
He said, I'm going to
give them so many days.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.080
As I remember, it was 21 days.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.970
And giving them exactly 21
days, right to the second,

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:22.630
he knew where each
one was in respect

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.460
to the sun or the stars.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.250
He'd know the
distances from the sun.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.890
By this time, he discovered
the moving in elliptical arcs.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.059
So he then had the radius
from the sun or the stars

00:14:33.059 --> 00:14:35.350
and then a different radius--
a little different radius

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.065
at the end of the 21 days.

00:14:37.065 --> 00:14:39.140
And he knew actually then.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:43.030
He was able to make a diagram
of each one of these new radius

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:45.190
and the elliptical arc.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:49.260
And having these pictures
now of triangles-- long,

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.812
thin triangles--

00:14:50.812 --> 00:14:53.280
he said, I have all the data.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:55.200
I might as well
calculate these areas.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:58.360
Well, there doesn't seem
to be any sort of triangles

00:14:58.360 --> 00:14:58.980
in the sky.

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.520
Might as well do that.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:03.630
And if you were Kepler and
then make this calculation

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.160
and discover they
were not similar,

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:08.790
but they were exactly the same,
think of it-- the astonishment

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:11.710
of a human being that
hidden in this great soup

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:15.040
of this disorder was an elegant
mathematical coordination.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.040
Because obviously it was
coordinated to come out

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.700
exactly the same-- all of them.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:21.322
So that you then have
to think in a way

00:15:21.322 --> 00:15:23.655
that you and I have never
have, and no other human being

00:15:23.655 --> 00:15:25.650
has ever had to think before.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.020
Because he doesn't tell
you this in his diary,

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:30.300
but supposing they were
touching each other,

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.040
he might understand
how they might

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.930
move like gears to coordinate.

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:36.570
But they were millions
of miles apart.

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:38.820
Millions of miles
apart, and human beings

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:40.780
had no idea of
anything operating

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:45.190
in millions of miles apart
in a tension and absolutely

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:49.020
invisible-- some kind of
invisible tendon operating it.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:49.520
Think of it.

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:52.170
Think of the intellectual
challenge that really was.

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:54.507
But he was familiar,
as a human being,

00:15:54.507 --> 00:15:56.340
that if you swing a
weight around your head,

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:57.240
it stays in orbit.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:00.910
If you let go, it
goes off in a line.

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:03.825
Also he has familiar, if you
wanted to make an ellipse,

00:16:03.825 --> 00:16:06.960
you have to use two restraints
instead of one restraint.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:10.065
So he had to assume
somehow or other--

00:16:10.065 --> 00:16:12.030
because he had found them
moving elliptically--

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:15.080
that there was some
kind of restraints

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:18.480
of tensions operating
over millions of miles.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:21.930
And the fact that the planets
bunched from time to time

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:23.910
may then possibly pull on--

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:28.330
the bunch could pull on the
one, as well as the sun.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:34.140
And he made those kind
of ordinary discoveries.

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:37.560
Now, here we have suddenly
some interrelationship existing

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:41.700
between that does not
manifest in any one of those.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:44.580
Nothing-- not any
one planet that

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:47.550
said there could be
strings to another planet,

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:49.540
as you'll get out of what
I'm talking about it.

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:52.880
Because there was a
group behaving this way

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.930
that humanity never
paid attention.

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:58.004
And finally when a
team behaving a little

00:16:58.004 --> 00:16:59.920
differently from all the
rest of the universe,

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:03.440
it finally discovers some
relationship going on there.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:06.680
We go on from there
to Galileo measuring

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:09.000
the rate of falling
bodies, acceleration

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.840
of the rate of
falling, and getting

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:11.839
the mathematics of that.

00:17:11.839 --> 00:17:14.599
And we have Isaac Newton
tremendously eager

00:17:14.599 --> 00:17:17.450
to understand what this
extraordinary, invisible

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:22.369
tension was that Kepler
had now discovered.

00:17:22.369 --> 00:17:25.160
And have Isaac
Newton then finally

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:29.216
being able to work out the fact
that the interrelationship,

00:17:29.216 --> 00:17:34.970
the interattractiveness,
was varying

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.730
as a second power,
mathematical distances apart,

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:39.050
but the inverse ratio of it.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:41.510
That is, if you halve the
distance between the two,

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:44.000
you increase to one-,
two-, four-fold.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.830
If you doubled the
distance apart,

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.500
it went down one
quarter of it before.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.350
Suddenly, we then
have a human mind

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:54.620
able to discover the
mathematical relationship--

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:57.550
which, firstly was hypothetical.

00:17:57.550 --> 00:17:59.930
But then as it's tested,
and tested, and tested back,

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:03.710
astronomers are always
explaining the interaction

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:05.750
of these celestial bodies--

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.910
whatever bodies you're studying.

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:09.700
So this rapidly
became what we call

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:13.520
a mathematical generalization--
a scientific generalization--

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.104
and found no
exceptions whatsoever.

00:18:16.104 --> 00:18:18.020
And it could only be
expressed mathematically.

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.330
So suddenly we
find the human mind

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:23.840
having a capability from time to
time to discover a relationship

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:27.570
existing between which can only
be expressed mathematically.

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:33.110
It's a highly intellectual
matter, and we have then--

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:35.450
I said brain dealing
in the special cases.

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:39.070
And then the special
cases were always

00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:41.910
temporal-- had
beginnings and endings.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:44.320
And what we have suddenly--
the human mind discovering

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:45.040
these principles.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.970
And as I say, if they qualify
as a generalized principle,

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:50.110
it means they have
no exceptions.

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:54.670
And that which has no exceptions
must be inherently eternal.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:57.490
Nothing to say that one
of these generalizations

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:00.140
may not someday prove
to have exceptions.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:03.310
But as far as we know, there
is a family of them today

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:05.010
which we have no exception.

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:08.140
Therefore, up to the time
we find the exception,

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:10.477
it must be considered
as inherently eternal.

00:19:10.477 --> 00:19:11.560
And that's very different.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:13.809
The human brain then asking
for beginnings and endings

00:19:13.809 --> 00:19:16.210
of the universe,
and the human mind

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.510
having capability to discover
that which is eternal.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:22.480
I became very intrigued
then by the idea

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:26.380
of what we call behaviors
of whole systems

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:31.170
like the planetary systems,
solar system, in which

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:34.060
the behavior of the
whole is not explained

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:37.960
by behavior of any of the powers
considered only separately.

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:39.140
We call that synergetic.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:42.820
So then I began to think about
the universe in those kinds

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:46.150
of terms and saying, how many
of these generalized principles

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:47.440
have we discovered?

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:48.850
As we discover
one, we don't know

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.016
we're going to discover it,
but suddenly we have it.

00:19:51.016 --> 00:19:52.570
Nor do we know
whether it's going

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:54.640
to be the last one that
would ever be discovered.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:56.540
We don't know how
many there are.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:20:01.490
But there is an
increasing inventory

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.080
There's a principle
of leverages,

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:04.960
the mathematics of that.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.790
And as Galileo
showed, you didn't

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:10.490
have to have a compression
lever and compression fulcrum.

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:12.260
You could have a
tension fulcrum.

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:16.690
You could have pulleys,
and falls counting out

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:19.090
the same mathematics.

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:22.630
So they are beautiful
mathematical laws

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:26.170
which are generalizations
that human beings could use

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:27.950
objectively as special cases.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.490
That then gave me an
odd feeling that humans

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:35.301
had a very different kind
of function in the universe.

00:20:35.301 --> 00:20:37.050
Because we didn't know
any other phenomena

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.775
that had access to these
extraordinary generalized

00:20:39.775 --> 00:20:40.320
principles.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:44.040
Because when you and
I use the word design,

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:48.660
we immediately would infer
an intellectual sorting and

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.899
deliberate arrangement.

00:20:50.899 --> 00:20:52.440
In other words, the
word design seems

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:56.390
to involve a complex of
that which is to be sorted

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.130
and to be arranged.

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:00.320
And the best we can see,
then, these human minds

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:03.210
have been discovering these
generalized principles.

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:05.310
And I said, what is very
impressive about them

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:07.760
is not only are they being
eternalized-- they're

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:10.540
all concurrently
operative-- but none of them

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:13.060
has ever been found to
contradict any of the others,

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:15.720
and several of them
are augmentative.

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:19.530
So in sum totally, a fine
human mind apparently

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:21.570
being admitted to some
of the great design

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:22.528
of the universe itself.

00:21:22.528 --> 00:21:24.065
I said, we must
be very important

00:21:24.065 --> 00:21:27.140
if we have kind of access.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.890
Therefore, we are now
trying to understand

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:31.015
why we're bound to this
planet and, we're thinking,

00:21:31.015 --> 00:21:33.585
bound to the universe itself.

00:21:33.585 --> 00:21:37.590
I also want you to think
about the extraordinary change

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:41.040
in the phenomena concept
of universe just in my day.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:47.314
When I was 28, Hubble
discovered another galaxy.

00:21:47.314 --> 00:21:48.570
Pretty extraordinary.

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:51.940
And we called it galaxy because
we had our galactic Milky

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:53.760
Way, our galactic system.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:55.010
And so there's another galaxy.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:58.102
And today, we know of
2 billion galaxies.

00:21:58.102 --> 00:21:59.810
So this will give you
an idea of the rate

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:03.770
of expansion of what you and I
have to consider as universe.

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:06.920
But you spontaneously today
think about the universe

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:09.440
as vastly greater than anything
I had to think about as.

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:13.880
Universe And this will
give you, again, a sense

00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:17.860
of the great,
incredible acceleration

00:22:17.860 --> 00:22:22.160
of knowing that's taking
place with humanity itself.

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:25.970
Now, thinking about that,
this function of humans

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:27.950
in the universe,
I also said, one

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:29.450
of the things that's
very impressive

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:33.080
is that human beings are
all born, always born,

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:36.850
naked, absolutely helpless for
months, beautiful equipment

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:40.300
but absolutely ignorant
because no experience.

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:42.640
So that we're deliberately
born that way,

00:22:42.640 --> 00:22:45.050
even though as our
eyes are designed,

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:46.760
our brain's designed
with a quadrillion

00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:49.640
atoms in coordinates, and
you and I can communicate.

00:22:49.640 --> 00:22:51.320
That's all a priori.

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:54.470
And so it's extraordinarily dumb
that we take it tremendously

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:56.350
for granted.

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:58.700
And it's only very
recently we begin

00:22:58.700 --> 00:23:02.420
to really take some kind
of cognizance so the fact

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:07.070
that this is such incredible
technology that we don't even

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:11.810
call it technology, because it's
way beyond the kind of grasp

00:23:11.810 --> 00:23:14.440
that humans so far
have of technology

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:18.080
and the kind of principles
we've employed up to date.

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:22.650
Now-- thinking now,
from this point on,

00:23:22.650 --> 00:23:25.840
I'm trying to identify why
humans are in the universe

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:30.670
and what we might be able to do
about carrying on abetting what

00:23:30.670 --> 00:23:33.700
nature, our universe-- why
does the universe have us

00:23:33.700 --> 00:23:39.380
here, and trying to abet the
realization of that function.

00:23:39.380 --> 00:23:40.760
In view of the
fact we are always

00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:44.170
born naked, helpless, and
ignorant, and the relatively

00:23:44.170 --> 00:23:47.340
short time we know of
our being on board here--

00:23:47.340 --> 00:23:49.480
for about 3 million years.

00:23:49.480 --> 00:23:52.600
It is amazing to me how
human beings then being

00:23:52.600 --> 00:23:58.000
born naked, helpless, ignorant,
but hungry, thirsty, curious,

00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:00.470
driven to make moves.

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:01.600
Hungry, trying out this.

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:04.850
And somebody eats a
berry, and they die.

00:24:04.850 --> 00:24:07.650
For then 1,000 years, that tribe
said nobody can eat berries.

00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:10.150
And then suddenly it discovered
there's some berries you can

00:24:10.150 --> 00:24:11.470
eat, some you couldn't.

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:16.540
And nature didn't have
any operating manual.

00:24:16.540 --> 00:24:18.910
She could perfectly well
have had green safe to eat

00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:20.930
and red dangerous to
eat if she wanted to.

00:24:20.930 --> 00:24:22.420
But she didn't do it that way.

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:26.170
She deliberately forced us
to learn by trial and error.

00:24:26.170 --> 00:24:29.120
That seemed to be a
deliberate part of the design.

00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:31.850
So that we've had to make an
incredible number of mistakes

00:24:31.850 --> 00:24:35.710
in those 3 million
years or more.

00:24:35.710 --> 00:24:37.990
And we've gotten
now to a point where

00:24:37.990 --> 00:24:40.660
we have discovered so many--

00:24:40.660 --> 00:24:43.990
150,000 nuances of
experience, which

00:24:43.990 --> 00:24:46.540
is so unique that they
require their own words,

00:24:46.540 --> 00:24:48.390
and we've agreed on those words.

00:24:48.390 --> 00:24:50.190
It's amazing matter
we've agreed that much,

00:24:50.190 --> 00:24:52.180
because agreements
are very different.

00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:55.960
So I found that here we
have an enormous facility

00:24:55.960 --> 00:24:58.050
of communication
with one another.

00:24:58.050 --> 00:25:01.576
And we suddenly have
come to a point where

00:25:01.576 --> 00:25:02.825
we did get that communication.

00:25:02.825 --> 00:25:06.539
And we then began to accumulate
information very, very rapidly.

00:25:06.539 --> 00:25:08.080
And I felt that all
of this had to do

00:25:08.080 --> 00:25:12.190
with all of us being born
in this sort of group

00:25:12.190 --> 00:25:14.860
womb of permitted ignorance,
with an enormous amount

00:25:14.860 --> 00:25:19.150
of resources by which we
could, by trial and error,

00:25:19.150 --> 00:25:21.870
learn something about why
we're here in the universe.

00:25:21.870 --> 00:25:25.240
And to me, then, is the most
absolutely important thing

00:25:25.240 --> 00:25:26.920
about us is our minds.

00:25:26.920 --> 00:25:30.400
Clearly, our muscle is nothing.

00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:32.630
We can't compete with a donkey.

00:25:32.630 --> 00:25:34.870
And we mean to get to
thinking about the energies

00:25:34.870 --> 00:25:43.771
in our universe that makes for
a rather quick summary of two

00:25:43.771 --> 00:25:44.270
things.

00:25:49.110 --> 00:25:53.150
As we know, during my lifetime
and just in this century,

00:25:53.150 --> 00:25:55.700
we began to discover that
chemical elements have

00:25:55.700 --> 00:25:58.600
unique frequencies
when incandescent

00:25:58.600 --> 00:26:02.750
in an arc frame which could be
detected by the spectroscope.

00:26:02.750 --> 00:26:08.030
And we have now,
using the light coming

00:26:08.030 --> 00:26:11.990
from the 2 billion
galaxies, we've

00:26:11.990 --> 00:26:15.020
been able to take that light and
run it through a spectroscope.

00:26:15.020 --> 00:26:16.970
And on one of our planets,
little human beings

00:26:16.970 --> 00:26:20.060
have an inventory of
the relative abundance

00:26:20.060 --> 00:26:23.270
of all the chemical
elements present within 11

00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:25.130
and 1/2 billion light
years around us.

00:26:25.130 --> 00:26:28.850
The human mind can has that
kind of scope and capability.

00:26:28.850 --> 00:26:30.730
But a muscle?

00:26:30.730 --> 00:26:31.730
Nothing.

00:26:31.730 --> 00:26:35.390
And yet muscle and
cunning are still

00:26:35.390 --> 00:26:37.652
in control of human affairs.

00:26:37.652 --> 00:26:40.890
So this is right why
we are in great peril.

00:26:40.890 --> 00:26:44.160
Because we're here quite
clearly for our minds, and minds

00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:46.940
are not in control.

00:26:46.940 --> 00:26:51.770
Now, I would come back to some
things that hit me very hard

00:26:51.770 --> 00:26:55.530
and are of great significance.

00:26:55.530 --> 00:27:00.740
For instance, in the Navy, where
I had been commander of a ship,

00:27:00.740 --> 00:27:04.340
and I had been so taught
that I could take over

00:27:04.340 --> 00:27:05.790
the job of my senior.

00:27:05.790 --> 00:27:08.210
I could take over the ship,
or I could take over the fleet

00:27:08.210 --> 00:27:09.620
if necessary.

00:27:09.620 --> 00:27:12.830
The whole training was that
way, all leading up to a moment

00:27:12.830 --> 00:27:15.140
of contact and destruction.

00:27:15.140 --> 00:27:18.320
I wondered how and why all
this extraordinary technology,

00:27:18.320 --> 00:27:20.620
beautiful science
had been reduced

00:27:20.620 --> 00:27:22.880
as to work to destruction.

00:27:22.880 --> 00:27:25.550
And this brought me,
then, to the discovery

00:27:25.550 --> 00:27:32.240
of the fact that for up to
1500, we'd been really thinking

00:27:32.240 --> 00:27:35.780
about all the universe
as a flat universe,

00:27:35.780 --> 00:27:38.150
even though there were
individuals who were quite

00:27:38.150 --> 00:27:40.350
sure our world was a sphere.

00:27:40.350 --> 00:27:42.380
But that was
anything but popular.

00:27:42.380 --> 00:27:43.880
The general way of
thinking about it

00:27:43.880 --> 00:27:46.010
was having a flat Earth.

00:27:46.010 --> 00:27:51.010
The Ptolemaic map, going
back really 3,000 years,

00:27:51.010 --> 00:27:52.030
was fitting.

00:27:52.030 --> 00:27:56.810
It took in all of Europe,
North Africa, and Asia

00:27:56.810 --> 00:27:59.155
in sort of a rectangular form.

00:27:59.155 --> 00:28:03.790
Then came to the wilderness
and went on to infinity.

00:28:03.790 --> 00:28:05.910
But it was a flat world.

00:28:05.910 --> 00:28:09.290
Now, this is true of
all the great empires--

00:28:09.290 --> 00:28:12.380
of Charlemagne, the Roman
Empire, you want anyone--

00:28:12.380 --> 00:28:14.015
Genghis Khan-- all
of those empires

00:28:14.015 --> 00:28:17.060
were these flat empires
going to infinity.

00:28:17.060 --> 00:28:20.450
And if you didn't like
the way things are,

00:28:20.450 --> 00:28:21.950
there are an infinite
number of gods

00:28:21.950 --> 00:28:22.830
and an infinite
number of chances

00:28:22.830 --> 00:28:24.663
that you'd come out all
right if you prayed.

00:28:24.663 --> 00:28:25.970
So it was worth praying.

00:28:25.970 --> 00:28:30.930
And we have suddenly
Magellan and discovering

00:28:30.930 --> 00:28:33.100
we're on a spherical earth.

00:28:33.100 --> 00:28:36.810
And we have the most powerful
people of these times,

00:28:36.810 --> 00:28:40.480
and learned that what we call
the control of the world wealth

00:28:40.480 --> 00:28:46.540
was by virtue of the controlling
of the great waterways.

00:28:46.540 --> 00:28:49.130
I'm going to-- I'd like
to extend that a little,

00:28:49.130 --> 00:28:51.170
because you are MIT.

00:28:51.170 --> 00:28:56.090
And we have the
archaeologically the city-state

00:28:56.090 --> 00:28:59.910
being discovered over and over
again-- in great walled cities.

00:28:59.910 --> 00:29:02.530
Mycenae in Greece is
a good example of it.

00:29:02.530 --> 00:29:05.020
There's a beautiful,
fertile valley, great rung

00:29:05.020 --> 00:29:06.320
around the mountains.

00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:09.040
In the middle is
a great high hill.

00:29:09.040 --> 00:29:13.400
And then on that high hill, you
could see all the passes coming

00:29:13.400 --> 00:29:16.205
into it, and you could look at
all the great fertile fields

00:29:16.205 --> 00:29:17.810
and command the whole show.

00:29:17.810 --> 00:29:20.330
And then you have, by
building great walls

00:29:20.330 --> 00:29:22.340
around the top of
that hill, and then

00:29:22.340 --> 00:29:26.800
walls going down to the well,
you had a very safe citadel.

00:29:26.800 --> 00:29:29.120
When you saw an enemy
coming, you then

00:29:29.120 --> 00:29:30.980
took all the foods
from the valley

00:29:30.980 --> 00:29:32.960
and brought them inside
the walls if you could.

00:29:32.960 --> 00:29:34.110
What you couldn't
bring in, you'd

00:29:34.110 --> 00:29:35.234
do what they call a scorch.

00:29:35.234 --> 00:29:36.200
You burn them up.

00:29:36.200 --> 00:29:39.110
So when the enemy came
in, all the local people

00:29:39.110 --> 00:29:41.950
had all their food inside,
and they had all their water.

00:29:41.950 --> 00:29:44.090
The people who came
were already hungry,

00:29:44.090 --> 00:29:46.237
and they could undergo
30 days without food

00:29:46.237 --> 00:29:47.570
without getting very, very weak.

00:29:47.570 --> 00:29:49.035
And then when they
get good and weak,

00:29:49.035 --> 00:29:50.410
you can go out
and decimate them.

00:29:50.410 --> 00:29:52.460
And this is why
the city-state was

00:29:52.460 --> 00:29:55.520
a very successful intervention
for thousands of years.

00:29:55.520 --> 00:29:57.540
In the meantime, human
beings began to build--

00:29:57.540 --> 00:29:59.660
well, 3/4 of Earth
is covered in water.

00:29:59.660 --> 00:30:02.960
Going from just
dugouts and rafts,

00:30:02.960 --> 00:30:05.309
and to suddenly getting
to ribbed ships.

00:30:05.309 --> 00:30:07.100
And the ribbed ships
got bigger and bigger,

00:30:07.100 --> 00:30:10.790
and got to the point of
about the time of Mycenae,

00:30:10.790 --> 00:30:11.930
or even Crete.

00:30:11.930 --> 00:30:14.812
And the Island of Crete,
there's no fortification,

00:30:14.812 --> 00:30:17.020
because this is the headquarters
of the water people.

00:30:17.020 --> 00:30:18.860
There's bigger and bigger boats.

00:30:18.860 --> 00:30:22.480
And we have then the Myceneans
going in their big boats

00:30:22.480 --> 00:30:23.600
up to Troy.

00:30:23.600 --> 00:30:28.160
And Troy, commandingly the
traffic from Asia into Europe--

00:30:28.160 --> 00:30:30.370
it was an extraordinarily
important point--

00:30:30.370 --> 00:30:31.970
complete with a walled city.

00:30:31.970 --> 00:30:33.470
So they have all
their food inside.

00:30:33.470 --> 00:30:35.450
When the enemy comes,
they expect the people

00:30:35.450 --> 00:30:36.740
outside to starve.

00:30:36.740 --> 00:30:39.110
But suddenly, there
were these great ships.

00:30:39.110 --> 00:30:41.120
They could go off and
get more supplies,

00:30:41.120 --> 00:30:43.350
continually brings supplies up.

00:30:43.350 --> 00:30:45.180
This is what we call
a line of supply.

00:30:45.180 --> 00:30:47.790
And then Troy fell.

00:30:47.790 --> 00:30:49.340
And then, from this
point on, history

00:30:49.340 --> 00:30:52.685
begins that where the great
and powerful people control,

00:30:52.685 --> 00:30:54.680
and the biggest control
is from controlling

00:30:54.680 --> 00:30:56.184
great lines of supply.

00:30:56.184 --> 00:30:58.850
This shows up very much when you
get to Italy, where you see all

00:30:58.850 --> 00:31:02.090
those beautiful, fertile
valleys with lovely castellos

00:31:02.090 --> 00:31:03.422
commanding the valleys.

00:31:03.422 --> 00:31:05.630
But there's one city in
Italy that's very different--

00:31:05.630 --> 00:31:06.350
Venice.

00:31:06.350 --> 00:31:08.960
And no walls whatsoever
because they're water people.

00:31:08.960 --> 00:31:12.126
And the water people then took
their ships all around Italy

00:31:12.126 --> 00:31:14.750
and brought up lines of supply,
and they starved all the people

00:31:14.750 --> 00:31:16.070
out of the castellos.

00:31:16.070 --> 00:31:18.870
This was a great change over in
the fundamentals of humanity.

00:31:18.870 --> 00:31:22.140
So we have suddenly Magellan
going around the world.

00:31:22.140 --> 00:31:28.220
And those who control the great
lines of supply between Europe

00:31:28.220 --> 00:31:30.980
and Asia, who has enormous
resources, great wealth

00:31:30.980 --> 00:31:33.770
had already been developed to
bring that wealth to Europe

00:31:33.770 --> 00:31:35.210
and cash in on it.

00:31:35.210 --> 00:31:36.980
Enormous ambitions to do that.

00:31:36.980 --> 00:31:38.930
These ambitions are
operated under the names

00:31:38.930 --> 00:31:40.940
of different countries
like France and Portugal,

00:31:40.940 --> 00:31:43.820
but they're really great,
powerful individuals.

00:31:43.820 --> 00:31:48.020
Queen Elizabeth I founds
the East India Company

00:31:48.020 --> 00:31:55.280
in 1600, about 3/4 of a century
after Magellan gets around.

00:31:55.280 --> 00:31:59.780
It was a private enterprise with
some of her private friends,

00:31:59.780 --> 00:32:04.930
and she was able to protect it
with her empire's capability.

00:32:04.930 --> 00:32:06.230
There's enormous battles.

00:32:06.230 --> 00:32:09.720
And by the Battle of
Trafalgar in 1805,

00:32:09.720 --> 00:32:12.680
suddenly British empire is it.

00:32:12.680 --> 00:32:15.260
And it's said to be the first
empire on which the sun never

00:32:15.260 --> 00:32:16.040
set.

00:32:16.040 --> 00:32:18.110
In order to carry on
and develop that empire,

00:32:18.110 --> 00:32:20.665
they also developed, then,
the East India Company College

00:32:20.665 --> 00:32:22.040
in England, which
is still there.

00:32:22.040 --> 00:32:24.630
The campus is still operating--
very beautiful campus.

00:32:24.630 --> 00:32:28.409
And on that campus in 1800,
writing just before Trafalgar--

00:32:28.409 --> 00:32:30.950
five years before and five years
after, two different books--

00:32:30.950 --> 00:32:34.140
you have Thomas Malthus, who
is a professor of economics

00:32:34.140 --> 00:32:36.310
at the East India
Company College.

00:32:36.310 --> 00:32:38.930
And he is the first
individual in history

00:32:38.930 --> 00:32:43.070
to have total vital statistics
from around a closed system

00:32:43.070 --> 00:32:45.200
earth, because the East
India Company contacts

00:32:45.200 --> 00:32:47.330
all these servants all
around the world picking up

00:32:47.330 --> 00:32:49.430
the critical information.

00:32:49.430 --> 00:32:52.190
So suddenly, he has this
incredible information,

00:32:52.190 --> 00:32:55.510
and he's able to write 1800,
and then 1810 to confirm it.

00:32:55.510 --> 00:32:58.430
And quite clearly, humanity
was multiplying itself

00:32:58.430 --> 00:33:01.560
at a geometrical rate,
producing life support only

00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:02.690
at an arithmetical rate.

00:33:02.690 --> 00:33:05.210
And quite clearly, the
majority of humanity's

00:33:05.210 --> 00:33:06.740
designed to be a failure.

00:33:06.740 --> 00:33:07.490
Pray all you want.

00:33:07.490 --> 00:33:08.364
It won't do any good.

00:33:08.364 --> 00:33:10.820
This isn't as it is anymore.

00:33:10.820 --> 00:33:13.441
So this is very formidable
piece of information

00:33:13.441 --> 00:33:14.690
for those who are in the know.

00:33:14.690 --> 00:33:17.776
But there was a
general illiteracy.

00:33:17.776 --> 00:33:19.400
It was not a popular
piece of knowledge

00:33:19.400 --> 00:33:21.410
at all as the
information of those

00:33:21.410 --> 00:33:24.710
who were in powerful positions
making very critical decisions

00:33:24.710 --> 00:33:25.800
for humanity.

00:33:25.800 --> 00:33:30.380
We have then, 35
years later, Darwin

00:33:30.380 --> 00:33:32.600
promulgating his
theory of evolution

00:33:32.600 --> 00:33:36.080
and suggesting that
survival only of the fittest

00:33:36.080 --> 00:33:38.480
is the fundamental cause of it.

00:33:38.480 --> 00:33:41.089
Then we have the economists
saying, all right.

00:33:41.089 --> 00:33:41.630
We like that.

00:33:41.630 --> 00:33:45.050
But Darwin said, I did not
develop this in economics.

00:33:45.050 --> 00:33:45.950
I did not mean it.

00:33:45.950 --> 00:33:48.380
But the economists said, well,
it fits our case perfectly.

00:33:48.380 --> 00:33:50.510
Then we have Karl
Marx in English

00:33:50.510 --> 00:33:54.920
saying he now accepts
Malthus as pure science,

00:33:54.920 --> 00:33:56.260
as a closed system.

00:33:56.260 --> 00:33:57.530
It's a closed system--

00:33:57.530 --> 00:33:58.910
hard fact.

00:33:58.910 --> 00:34:01.520
And we have Darwin, survival
only of the fittest.

00:34:01.520 --> 00:34:05.480
So Karl Marx said quite
clearly, the worker

00:34:05.480 --> 00:34:07.190
is fittest survive
because he knows

00:34:07.190 --> 00:34:09.496
how to handle the tools
to make all the products,

00:34:09.496 --> 00:34:10.870
how to grow the
seeds and things.

00:34:10.870 --> 00:34:12.246
These other people
are parasites.

00:34:12.246 --> 00:34:14.453
The other people said, we're
obviously not parasites.

00:34:14.453 --> 00:34:16.580
We're at the top of the
heap because the workers

00:34:16.580 --> 00:34:19.250
are so dull, we need some really
bright people around here.

00:34:19.250 --> 00:34:24.469
Make some kind of long distance,
visionary speculations.

00:34:24.469 --> 00:34:27.915
So we have then, since
that time, a closed system

00:34:27.915 --> 00:34:30.429
Earth instead of a flat Earth.

00:34:30.429 --> 00:34:32.219
Rather, suddenly
instead of being

00:34:32.219 --> 00:34:35.060
a dichotomy of different
kind of religions,

00:34:35.060 --> 00:34:38.350
we have the socialist
and the viewpoint

00:34:38.350 --> 00:34:43.134
and the out and out enterprise.

00:34:43.134 --> 00:34:45.830
There's various degrees
between the two,

00:34:45.830 --> 00:34:49.659
but we have since that
time on our planet,

00:34:49.659 --> 00:34:52.699
the great ideologies
saying you may not

00:34:52.699 --> 00:34:54.560
like our system
personally, but we're

00:34:54.560 --> 00:34:57.590
convinced we have the
fairest, most logical,

00:34:57.590 --> 00:35:01.150
most ingenious way of coping
with vessel inadequacy of life

00:35:01.150 --> 00:35:02.180
support.

00:35:02.180 --> 00:35:04.730
But because there are those
who disagree diametrically

00:35:04.730 --> 00:35:08.120
on how to cope, it can only
be resolved by trial of arms.

00:35:08.120 --> 00:35:10.800
Which system is
fittest to survive?

00:35:10.800 --> 00:35:12.300
And that's the
reason, for instance,

00:35:12.300 --> 00:35:15.770
that Russia and the United
States for the last 30 years

00:35:15.770 --> 00:35:18.680
have been appropriating
over $200 billion a year--

00:35:18.680 --> 00:35:22.520
sum total now over $6 trillion--
have been appropriating,

00:35:22.520 --> 00:35:24.810
so buying the highest
capability of humanity

00:35:24.810 --> 00:35:27.830
and focus it on how to
destroy most accurately, most

00:35:27.830 --> 00:35:30.096
effectively, at greater and
greater distances, swifter

00:35:30.096 --> 00:35:32.760
and swifter.

00:35:32.760 --> 00:35:36.340
This seems like an incredibly
poor investment of all

00:35:36.340 --> 00:35:38.156
that we've really
learned, then, right?

00:35:38.156 --> 00:35:39.130
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:35:39.130 --> 00:35:40.421
FULLER: That's where it's gone.

00:35:40.421 --> 00:35:47.149
AUDIENCE: [APPLAUSE]

00:35:47.149 --> 00:35:48.440
FULLER: I'm worried about time.

00:35:48.440 --> 00:35:50.148
I'm trying to think
how to get everything

00:35:50.148 --> 00:35:54.422
I really need to get to in the
shortest numbers of minutes.

00:35:54.422 --> 00:36:01.310
Anyway, what I had begun
to experience-- as I said,

00:36:01.310 --> 00:36:03.590
here I am in Cambridge
as a little boy,

00:36:03.590 --> 00:36:06.530
and I'm suddenly having
this wireless come in,

00:36:06.530 --> 00:36:10.430
suddenly the
airplanes coming in.

00:36:10.430 --> 00:36:16.760
I said, I really feel something.

00:36:16.760 --> 00:36:20.690
And what was really
coming in was from what

00:36:20.690 --> 00:36:23.842
I call a visible reality.

00:36:23.842 --> 00:36:25.550
Reality, when I was
young, was everything

00:36:25.550 --> 00:36:27.820
you could see, smell,
touch, and hear.

00:36:27.820 --> 00:36:29.200
That's reality.

00:36:29.200 --> 00:36:33.970
And they said, if you're a
sane man, and you're healthy,

00:36:33.970 --> 00:36:37.540
you knew just what you're doing.

00:36:37.540 --> 00:36:39.010
Suddenly, this is
upset very much

00:36:39.010 --> 00:36:41.582
by Freud and Mesmer discovering
a great many things we

00:36:41.582 --> 00:36:43.540
didn't know, but we're
still doing them anyway.

00:36:43.540 --> 00:36:44.373
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:36:44.373 --> 00:36:47.407
FULLER: But when I was young, it
was really exactly what I sad.

00:36:47.407 --> 00:36:49.990
You knew just what you're doing
if you can smell it, touch it,

00:36:49.990 --> 00:36:52.210
see it, and hear it, can't you?

00:36:52.210 --> 00:36:54.680
Now, I realized something
was coming in which

00:36:54.680 --> 00:36:56.480
I call an invisible reality.

00:36:56.480 --> 00:36:59.867
Because suddenly, when I
was three years of age,

00:36:59.867 --> 00:37:00.950
electrons were discovered.

00:37:00.950 --> 00:37:02.158
It didn't make any newspaper.

00:37:02.158 --> 00:37:04.520
Nobody knew that's
going to be anything.

00:37:04.520 --> 00:37:08.080
And suddenly there
were these alloys.

00:37:08.080 --> 00:37:12.710
And we're suddenly bringing,
by really accident--

00:37:12.710 --> 00:37:16.910
all the great alloy
discoveries by metallurgists

00:37:16.910 --> 00:37:20.180
have been really accidental
up to the time of the space

00:37:20.180 --> 00:37:23.220
program after World War II.

00:37:23.220 --> 00:37:26.330
And so we had, them, alloys.

00:37:26.330 --> 00:37:28.040
And an alloy--

00:37:28.040 --> 00:37:30.540
I'll just give you in
terms of aluminum, which

00:37:30.540 --> 00:37:33.170
is very dramatically clear.

00:37:33.170 --> 00:37:36.140
Aluminum is where we learned
to refine electrolytically only

00:37:36.140 --> 00:37:39.050
in the '90s, but we
don't really use it

00:37:39.050 --> 00:37:43.250
for anything but a souvenir,
as ashtrays, and things

00:37:43.250 --> 00:37:45.770
like that up to the
1930s when it goes

00:37:45.770 --> 00:37:47.750
in the airplane for first time.

00:37:47.750 --> 00:37:51.250
And the aluminum,
and what we use

00:37:51.250 --> 00:37:56.860
as the obvious property
giving the greatest

00:37:56.860 --> 00:37:58.790
clue to the strength
of material,

00:37:58.790 --> 00:38:02.350
is the ability to go here
and not be pulled apart.

00:38:02.350 --> 00:38:04.610
And so we call it a tensile
strength per square inch

00:38:04.610 --> 00:38:06.860
or whatever section we want.

00:38:06.860 --> 00:38:09.870
And so the tensile
strength of pure aluminum

00:38:09.870 --> 00:38:12.980
is 18,000 pounds
per square inch.

00:38:12.980 --> 00:38:14.750
We learned then, accidentally--

00:38:14.750 --> 00:38:16.720
a little copper got
into and so forth--

00:38:16.720 --> 00:38:20.780
and it got up suddenly to
double that strength of 36,000.

00:38:20.780 --> 00:38:22.381
Then during World
War II, the Japanese

00:38:22.381 --> 00:38:23.880
brought in another
alloy that got up

00:38:23.880 --> 00:38:27.250
to 72,000 pounds
per square inch.

00:38:27.250 --> 00:38:29.990
So I could have three
rods of aluminum

00:38:29.990 --> 00:38:33.360
here, one inch in diameter,
say three feet long, all

00:38:33.360 --> 00:38:34.420
the way the same.

00:38:34.420 --> 00:38:37.560
No scientists can look at them,
tell any difference whatsoever,

00:38:37.560 --> 00:38:40.780
and this one is double of
this, and this is double again.

00:38:40.780 --> 00:38:44.050
Now, here was something
coming into World War I

00:38:44.050 --> 00:38:48.860
that I, being a
regular line officer,

00:38:48.860 --> 00:38:51.350
became tremendously aware of.

00:38:51.350 --> 00:38:53.887
And up to this
time, everybody knew

00:38:53.887 --> 00:38:56.470
that spies could see the size
of the ships they were building.

00:38:56.470 --> 00:38:58.340
It took a long time
to build a ship.

00:38:58.340 --> 00:38:59.923
You could take, then,
the total cubage

00:38:59.923 --> 00:39:02.760
of the weight of that
water, that cubage of water

00:39:02.760 --> 00:39:05.930
was all the ship could weigh,
everything had on board.

00:39:05.930 --> 00:39:11.030
But suddenly, I saw in World War
I that a ship is coming at you

00:39:11.030 --> 00:39:14.080
and has the same
tonnage as your ship,

00:39:14.080 --> 00:39:17.097
has the same number of
guns, the same size guns.

00:39:17.097 --> 00:39:18.680
But yet, this you
don't know, and it's

00:39:18.680 --> 00:39:21.190
coming at you, that its metal
is much stronger in the front,

00:39:21.190 --> 00:39:23.610
and it can fire
much further away.

00:39:23.610 --> 00:39:26.900
And this became the most highly
classified secret information

00:39:26.900 --> 00:39:29.000
in World War I, was the alloys.

00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:33.207
And suddenly we had
an invisible reality.

00:39:33.207 --> 00:39:34.790
And the public
couldn't tell about it.

00:39:34.790 --> 00:39:37.580
It's very easy to keep a
secret in complete ignorancy

00:39:37.580 --> 00:39:38.900
and no way to understand.

00:39:38.900 --> 00:39:42.350
So one ship went to the bottom,
of they couldn't tell anything

00:39:42.350 --> 00:39:43.020
about it.

00:39:43.020 --> 00:39:45.320
And so it is very easy
keeping that kind of secret.

00:39:45.320 --> 00:39:46.153
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:39:46.153 --> 00:39:49.800
FULLER: So I became
fascinated, then,

00:39:49.800 --> 00:39:53.280
in World War I to
realize that we're

00:39:53.280 --> 00:39:57.002
beginning to do more with
the same and more with less.

00:39:57.002 --> 00:39:59.210
And I could see it was coming
in many different ways.

00:39:59.210 --> 00:40:02.929
In electronics--
Malthaus didn't know.

00:40:02.929 --> 00:40:05.345
He assumed if you had a message
to go across the Atlantic,

00:40:05.345 --> 00:40:06.520
you had to send a ship.

00:40:06.520 --> 00:40:09.084
It was going to
take 40, 50 days.

00:40:09.084 --> 00:40:11.125
He didn't know I had a
little piece of apparatus.

00:40:11.125 --> 00:40:15.992
that I could do it at
186,000 miles a second.

00:40:15.992 --> 00:40:17.950
I said, how many things
did Malthaus leave out?

00:40:17.950 --> 00:40:19.610
So I began to keep lists of it.

00:40:19.610 --> 00:40:24.170
By 1917, really late 1917,
I'd become really excited

00:40:24.170 --> 00:40:28.120
to realize there was something
going on in humanity which

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:30.620
had me intuitively
curious anyway,

00:40:30.620 --> 00:40:33.470
where we're doing more
with less invisibly.

00:40:33.470 --> 00:40:36.530
And might be someday that you
do so much with so little,

00:40:36.530 --> 00:40:39.700
it might be possible
that Malthaus was wrong.

00:40:39.700 --> 00:40:42.530
It might be enough for everybody
if we did it enough of it.

00:40:42.530 --> 00:40:44.960
This was a terribly
challenging idea

00:40:44.960 --> 00:40:47.667
as a kid to really get in
to see it could be true.

00:40:47.667 --> 00:40:50.000
I came out of the Navy and
went into the building world.

00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:51.958
I stayed in that building
world for five years,

00:40:51.958 --> 00:40:54.680
and I found it
thousands of years

00:40:54.680 --> 00:40:56.900
behind the arts of the
environment controlling

00:40:56.900 --> 00:40:59.420
of the sea and the sky.

00:40:59.420 --> 00:41:03.350
I just wanted to point out, too,
how you talk about how much--

00:41:03.350 --> 00:41:07.370
you know exactly what a
Boeing 747 weighs, loaded--

00:41:07.370 --> 00:41:10.046
three tons-- and her rate of
climb, how many people she

00:41:10.046 --> 00:41:10.546
can carry.

00:41:10.546 --> 00:41:13.140
You know everything she can do
out of every pound of material

00:41:13.140 --> 00:41:16.910
you put in, every ounce of
materials, every erg of energy,

00:41:16.910 --> 00:41:18.692
every second of time.

00:41:18.692 --> 00:41:20.650
But you ask if you people
what buildings weigh,

00:41:20.650 --> 00:41:22.375
they don't know what
the buildings weigh.

00:41:22.375 --> 00:41:24.080
If you don't know
what buildings weigh,

00:41:24.080 --> 00:41:26.288
you certainly don't have
any way to ratio performance

00:41:26.288 --> 00:41:28.370
or just want to get an
idea of the building world

00:41:28.370 --> 00:41:30.620
on the land being thousands
of years behind that

00:41:30.620 --> 00:41:32.120
of the sea and the sky.

00:41:32.120 --> 00:41:35.450
We know exactly what you're
getting out of every ounce.

00:41:35.450 --> 00:41:38.260
You have to know.

00:41:38.260 --> 00:41:42.050
So I became excited to realize
that it was in the building

00:41:42.050 --> 00:41:44.480
world that we're really
behind, because there

00:41:44.480 --> 00:41:48.620
was something called priorities
in relation to the military.

00:41:48.620 --> 00:41:50.300
If these heads of
state, then, are

00:41:50.300 --> 00:41:52.040
going to have to
protect themselves

00:41:52.040 --> 00:41:54.867
against other states, they're
going to defend themselves.

00:41:54.867 --> 00:41:56.200
There's not enough to go around.

00:41:56.200 --> 00:41:57.710
They've been told that.

00:41:57.710 --> 00:42:00.350
Then they leave things to
the military to defend them.

00:42:00.350 --> 00:42:02.450
The military will
say, well, all right.

00:42:02.450 --> 00:42:05.500
We now know that there are
these chemical elements.

00:42:05.500 --> 00:42:08.325
And there's so much mercury,
and there's so much helium.

00:42:08.325 --> 00:42:09.950
And they do something
absolutely unique

00:42:09.950 --> 00:42:11.510
that nothing else could do.

00:42:11.510 --> 00:42:13.970
Who has access to these
absolutely unique, high

00:42:13.970 --> 00:42:15.770
performance materials?

00:42:15.770 --> 00:42:19.670
Who has access to the
unique, very high performance

00:42:19.670 --> 00:42:23.060
of special instruments and
tools, production tools

00:42:23.060 --> 00:42:25.295
made by well-trained brains?

00:42:25.295 --> 00:42:29.240
Obviously, then, you
have priority of access

00:42:29.240 --> 00:42:31.500
to the high performance
capabilities.

00:42:31.500 --> 00:42:32.417
The military had that.

00:42:32.417 --> 00:42:34.166
This meant then that
if you have priority,

00:42:34.166 --> 00:42:35.840
you have to have anti-priority.

00:42:35.840 --> 00:42:38.391
Who has to make do with the low
performance or no performance

00:42:38.391 --> 00:42:38.890
at all?

00:42:38.890 --> 00:42:40.490
It was obviously the home front.

00:42:40.490 --> 00:42:42.140
There's not enough
for people anyway.

00:42:42.140 --> 00:42:44.120
Let the poor devils get
on the best they can.

00:42:44.120 --> 00:42:46.860
So human beings
being human beings

00:42:46.860 --> 00:42:48.920
and trying to make
the best of life,

00:42:48.920 --> 00:42:52.170
did get up in architecture
that was, to them, at least

00:42:52.170 --> 00:42:54.440
attractive out of the make do.

00:42:54.440 --> 00:42:57.320
Where we have then the bigger
heavier, the thicker the wall,

00:42:57.320 --> 00:42:58.770
more secure.

00:42:58.770 --> 00:43:01.790
That idea went out
in architecture

00:43:01.790 --> 00:43:05.366
along with the Maginot Line.

00:43:05.366 --> 00:43:07.180
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:43:07.180 --> 00:43:09.970
FULLER: And right up to then,
you consoled yourself that way.

00:43:09.970 --> 00:43:11.428
The bigger, and
heavier, and higher

00:43:11.428 --> 00:43:12.620
the walls, the more secure.

00:43:12.620 --> 00:43:14.040
We used to have all
the advertisement

00:43:14.040 --> 00:43:16.039
when I was young about a
great insurance company

00:43:16.039 --> 00:43:20.290
with, Safe as the
Rock of Gibraltar.

00:43:20.290 --> 00:43:22.091
They don't use that
advertisement anymore.

00:43:22.091 --> 00:43:22.590
No.

00:43:22.590 --> 00:43:23.970
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:43:23.970 --> 00:43:27.700
FULLER: Now, what
excited me in 1927--

00:43:27.700 --> 00:43:29.610
I'd been in this
building world and found

00:43:29.610 --> 00:43:31.570
that no scientists
ever had even been

00:43:31.570 --> 00:43:33.070
asked to look at the plumbing.

00:43:33.070 --> 00:43:34.900
Just think of it.

00:43:34.900 --> 00:43:37.540
No scientist has ever done
anything about the plumbing.

00:43:37.540 --> 00:43:41.852
You have beautiful
courses here on frictions

00:43:41.852 --> 00:43:43.560
in pipes and things
like that, but nobody

00:43:43.560 --> 00:43:46.050
is redesigning the plumbing.

00:43:46.050 --> 00:43:48.280
Here we have the human
beings, every one

00:43:48.280 --> 00:43:53.570
of you, several times a day
taking this beautiful sun

00:43:53.570 --> 00:43:56.080
evaporation, water getting
in the sky and coming down

00:43:56.080 --> 00:43:57.665
and absolutely pure to us.

00:43:57.665 --> 00:43:59.040
And we take that
beautiful water,

00:43:59.040 --> 00:44:02.880
and we use four and five
gallons several times a day

00:44:02.880 --> 00:44:05.064
to get rid of a pint of yellow.

00:44:05.064 --> 00:44:06.852
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:44:06.852 --> 00:44:09.556
FULLER: How much
sense does that make?

00:44:09.556 --> 00:44:13.930
And they'd just
say, the home front

00:44:13.930 --> 00:44:15.750
was absolutely
thousands of years

00:44:15.750 --> 00:44:18.270
behind the art of
the sea and the sky.

00:44:18.270 --> 00:44:23.250
So in 1927, the American
Institute of Architects,

00:44:23.250 --> 00:44:25.711
as they do today,
had their journal.

00:44:25.711 --> 00:44:27.210
And in their journal,
they published

00:44:27.210 --> 00:44:28.920
buildings they thought well of.

00:44:28.920 --> 00:44:31.500
And they had a single
family dwelling in Illinois

00:44:31.500 --> 00:44:33.990
in 1927 which they
thought was optimum

00:44:33.990 --> 00:44:37.020
for under the
conditions of 1927.

00:44:37.020 --> 00:44:40.560
I took that total floor area,
total cubage, total number

00:44:40.560 --> 00:44:43.380
of windows and lumens of light
that could get in, everything

00:44:43.380 --> 00:44:45.990
it had equipment to do,
listed all the performance

00:44:45.990 --> 00:44:47.280
capabilities.

00:44:47.280 --> 00:44:49.710
And I took its total weight,
including the pipes out

00:44:49.710 --> 00:44:50.370
to the mains.

00:44:50.370 --> 00:44:52.920
It came out 150 tons.

00:44:52.920 --> 00:44:58.030
Then having to match the
same cubage, same floor area,

00:44:58.030 --> 00:45:01.230
every performance capability
of the single family

00:45:01.230 --> 00:45:04.410
dwelling, Illinois, but using
the most advanced aircraft

00:45:04.410 --> 00:45:08.000
design of the time, it
came out only three tons.

00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:10.500
So I said, three
tons against 150.

00:45:10.500 --> 00:45:12.330
If we really began,
instead of waiting,

00:45:12.330 --> 00:45:14.670
which was going
on in those days.

00:45:14.670 --> 00:45:19.115
I saw after the military
developed something,

00:45:19.115 --> 00:45:20.490
then suddenly it
became obsolete.

00:45:20.490 --> 00:45:23.170
They had to take the
weapon, and people

00:45:23.170 --> 00:45:26.160
who were all tooled up to
produce this kind of equipment,

00:45:26.160 --> 00:45:28.400
then look around the home
front for some outlets.

00:45:28.400 --> 00:45:30.830
This is how the process
of the refrigeration which

00:45:30.830 --> 00:45:33.420
it had in the navy
for 25 years suddenly

00:45:33.420 --> 00:45:35.820
came up on the land in
the '20s, and suddenly you

00:45:35.820 --> 00:45:38.160
didn't have to have
ice in your box there.

00:45:38.160 --> 00:45:40.140
And so I saw
there's fallout that

00:45:40.140 --> 00:45:43.020
came very secondarily,
very laggardly,

00:45:43.020 --> 00:45:45.774
maybe a quarter of a century,
maybe half a century later,

00:45:45.774 --> 00:45:47.190
came into the home
front and began

00:45:47.190 --> 00:45:49.070
to change the
standard of living.

00:45:49.070 --> 00:45:51.270
In the terms of
which, yes, in my day,

00:45:51.270 --> 00:45:53.900
we've gone from less
than 1% of humanity

00:45:53.900 --> 00:45:57.930
to 56% of humanity enjoying
a higher standard of living

00:45:57.930 --> 00:46:01.260
today than was known or
expected by any potentate when

00:46:01.260 --> 00:46:02.270
I was born.

00:46:02.270 --> 00:46:04.436
And during that time, we've
doubled the population--

00:46:04.436 --> 00:46:08.430
so actually have 112-folded
the number being benefited

00:46:08.430 --> 00:46:09.750
by advanced technology.

00:46:09.750 --> 00:46:12.570
But all this was a
very slow feedback

00:46:12.570 --> 00:46:16.170
from the preoccupation
with how to kill.

00:46:16.170 --> 00:46:18.580
So I said, supposing we
didn't wait for that,

00:46:18.580 --> 00:46:20.270
but looked at the
home front right away.

00:46:23.430 --> 00:46:26.960
I was indicated by this
three tons against 150

00:46:26.960 --> 00:46:30.040
that maybe we could really get
doing so much with so little,

00:46:30.040 --> 00:46:32.350
we could really demonstrate
to humanity there really

00:46:32.350 --> 00:46:33.860
is enough to go around.

00:46:33.860 --> 00:46:38.540
So that was 52 years ago, and I
have engaged in that direction

00:46:38.540 --> 00:46:39.040
ever since.

00:46:39.040 --> 00:46:41.380
Then and now that
brought me across into

00:46:41.380 --> 00:46:44.035
geodesic structures,
where I could do very much

00:46:44.035 --> 00:46:45.420
more with very much less.

00:46:45.420 --> 00:46:47.230
There are now over
200,000 of them

00:46:47.230 --> 00:46:48.680
somewhere around the world.

00:46:48.680 --> 00:46:51.790
They're in remote places
where the very highest kind

00:46:51.790 --> 00:46:54.700
of performance is required,
where other kinds of structures

00:46:54.700 --> 00:46:57.190
just would not do, whether
they're ringing in the DEW line

00:46:57.190 --> 00:47:02.300
with radios or the experimental
station over the South Pole,

00:47:02.300 --> 00:47:05.800
or whether radar on
top of Mount Fuji able

00:47:05.800 --> 00:47:08.320
to withstand the most
extraordinary hurricanes

00:47:08.320 --> 00:47:10.940
and gales, snow loads.

00:47:10.940 --> 00:47:14.100
So delicate that microwaves
can go through, yet so light

00:47:14.100 --> 00:47:15.770
that one helicopter
took it up there

00:47:15.770 --> 00:47:19.430
and fastened it in place
like a great bird landing.

00:47:19.430 --> 00:47:21.715
So I've had enough
experience in the logistics

00:47:21.715 --> 00:47:24.610
of environment controlling.

00:47:24.610 --> 00:47:28.010
And due to the factor also,
I've been counting on,

00:47:28.010 --> 00:47:32.270
since 1927, what I
call the World Game.

00:47:32.270 --> 00:47:36.960
Instead of the navy
game of World War games

00:47:36.960 --> 00:47:38.960
where the people in the
land were not concerned,

00:47:38.960 --> 00:47:41.780
but the Navy was concerned
because 3/4 of this is water.

00:47:41.780 --> 00:47:45.785
And then who's going to get
control of the line of supply?

00:47:45.785 --> 00:47:47.690
That's the whole the story.

00:47:47.690 --> 00:47:49.982
And how many resources are
there around the world?

00:47:49.982 --> 00:47:52.190
Whole training of the navy
was to learn those things.

00:47:52.190 --> 00:47:54.870
And now I said, I'm going to
play a game called World Game

00:47:54.870 --> 00:47:58.310
not World War Game, where
I look at the sum total

00:47:58.310 --> 00:48:01.130
and see how I can use it, if
possible, to make all humanity

00:48:01.130 --> 00:48:02.870
a success.

00:48:02.870 --> 00:48:06.770
It seemed to be indicated
as implicit in this trending

00:48:06.770 --> 00:48:08.650
of doing more with less.

00:48:08.650 --> 00:48:13.028
Now, so I've kept
all kinds of curves.

00:48:13.028 --> 00:48:14.736
I kept the curves of
the rate of increase

00:48:14.736 --> 00:48:16.460
of the tensile
strengths in the steals,

00:48:16.460 --> 00:48:18.830
and then got into the aluminum.

00:48:18.830 --> 00:48:21.800
I found that I could predict the
aluminum curve would follow it.

00:48:21.800 --> 00:48:23.540
And it did, et
cetera, et cetera.

00:48:23.540 --> 00:48:27.020
And by keeping enough track
of all the total data,

00:48:27.020 --> 00:48:30.500
I've been able then to be able
to say certain things back.

00:48:30.500 --> 00:48:34.940
10 years ago, I was
able then, by actually,

00:48:34.940 --> 00:48:40.660
design, able to say it
is now incontrovertibly

00:48:40.660 --> 00:48:44.740
evidencable in engineering
that we within 10 years

00:48:44.740 --> 00:48:51.810
have a design revolution where
using only proven technology,

00:48:51.810 --> 00:48:54.855
using only metals already
mined that are recirculating,

00:48:54.855 --> 00:48:56.920
it's perfectly feasible
within 10 years

00:48:56.920 --> 00:48:59.580
to have all humanity
living at a higher

00:48:59.580 --> 00:49:02.220
standard of living than any
humans have ever known before--

00:49:02.220 --> 00:49:03.510
on a sustainable basis.

00:49:03.510 --> 00:49:05.760
Because during
that same 10 years,

00:49:05.760 --> 00:49:09.080
we can phase out forever all
further use of fossil fuels

00:49:09.080 --> 00:49:10.230
and atomic energy.

00:49:10.230 --> 00:49:13.020
We can live entirely
on our energy income.

00:49:13.020 --> 00:49:16.700
Now, this became, as I say,
incontrovertibly demonstrable.

00:49:16.700 --> 00:49:19.540
For instance, just
take the energy side.

00:49:19.540 --> 00:49:24.710
We have a book which is
published by our World Game,

00:49:24.710 --> 00:49:26.500
Energy, Earth, and Everyone.

00:49:26.500 --> 00:49:30.520
You'll be able to get copies
of it from Doubleday in July.

00:49:30.520 --> 00:49:32.560
The first printings
were exhausted,

00:49:32.560 --> 00:49:36.450
and the title went from
the Straight Arrow Press

00:49:36.450 --> 00:49:38.230
in San Francisco to
Simon and Schuster,

00:49:38.230 --> 00:49:39.340
who sold it to Doubleday.

00:49:39.340 --> 00:49:41.506
And Doubleday has been very
slow on bringing it out,

00:49:41.506 --> 00:49:43.270
but it will be out in July.

00:49:43.270 --> 00:49:46.070
You'll find absolute
incontrovertible ability

00:49:46.070 --> 00:49:48.050
to live on our energy income.

00:49:48.050 --> 00:49:51.460
And incidentally, I'd just like
to mention the following to you

00:49:51.460 --> 00:49:54.120
as a world of technology.

00:49:54.120 --> 00:49:58.240
In World War II, the grand
strategy against Hitler

00:49:58.240 --> 00:50:00.194
was then to cut off his energy.

00:50:00.194 --> 00:50:02.360
And they were able to then
bomb Ploesti and so forth

00:50:02.360 --> 00:50:03.445
immediately.

00:50:03.445 --> 00:50:06.040
The German scientists
went to work,

00:50:06.040 --> 00:50:08.110
and they learned how to
keep their economy going

00:50:08.110 --> 00:50:11.530
on their energy income
entirely from the vegetation.

00:50:11.530 --> 00:50:14.950
They were able then, to, go
into the four kinds of alcohol

00:50:14.950 --> 00:50:16.870
to Grand Central
Station of energy.

00:50:16.870 --> 00:50:18.396
And from there, they could get--

00:50:18.396 --> 00:50:19.770
you may have
remembered they also

00:50:19.770 --> 00:50:23.220
developed the very high
performance rubber, where

00:50:23.220 --> 00:50:26.620
instead of having the 10,000
mile tires, got up to 50,000.

00:50:26.620 --> 00:50:29.000
And they did this
all on alcohol.

00:50:29.000 --> 00:50:30.670
All coming entirely
from vegetation,

00:50:30.670 --> 00:50:33.800
they were able then to produce
high octane gas, gasoline.

00:50:33.800 --> 00:50:35.830
They were able to produce food.

00:50:35.830 --> 00:50:37.680
And they kept their
economy going.

00:50:37.680 --> 00:50:41.250
It's very amazing to me that
the United States rushing in

00:50:41.250 --> 00:50:42.930
as they did in Berlin--

00:50:42.930 --> 00:50:44.980
and because I was in the
broader economic world,

00:50:44.980 --> 00:50:46.547
and I know we had all that data.

00:50:46.547 --> 00:50:48.130
None of this data
had been brought out

00:50:48.130 --> 00:50:50.500
and the energy mentioned to you.

00:50:50.500 --> 00:50:52.750
I want you realize that
there's-- why didn't that come

00:50:52.750 --> 00:50:53.849
out?

00:50:53.849 --> 00:50:55.390
Well, the next thing
I've discovered,

00:50:55.390 --> 00:50:57.723
having made a statement such
as I have just made to you,

00:50:57.723 --> 00:50:59.630
I'd been able to
make it 10 years ago

00:50:59.630 --> 00:51:03.100
and have been making
it publicly ever since.

00:51:03.100 --> 00:51:05.290
You get checked up
at such statements.

00:51:05.290 --> 00:51:08.770
And possibly over a thousand
really quite confident people

00:51:08.770 --> 00:51:11.140
have checked over my
data found it's correct.

00:51:11.140 --> 00:51:15.699
It may be about a million people
who have credited those 1,000.

00:51:15.699 --> 00:51:17.240
But there are 4
billion human beings,

00:51:17.240 --> 00:51:18.960
so humanity doesn't know this.

00:51:18.960 --> 00:51:20.550
But there is an
increasing number

00:51:20.550 --> 00:51:22.600
who know that it's possible.

00:51:22.600 --> 00:51:28.650
Now, the next thing I discovered
was that all big government--

00:51:28.650 --> 00:51:30.680
which is political--

00:51:30.680 --> 00:51:35.290
all big politics, all big
religion, all big business

00:51:35.290 --> 00:51:37.960
found it absolutely
devastating an activity

00:51:37.960 --> 00:51:39.104
to have humanity a success.

00:51:39.104 --> 00:51:41.270
They're all predicated on
humanity being in trouble.

00:51:41.270 --> 00:51:47.850
AUDIENCE: [APPLAUSE]

00:51:47.850 --> 00:51:48.720
FULLER: Come to me.

00:51:48.720 --> 00:51:49.595
Join our side.

00:51:49.595 --> 00:51:51.136
We can get you a
little better deals.

00:51:51.136 --> 00:51:52.050
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:51:52.050 --> 00:51:53.570
FULLER: You're poor people.

00:51:53.570 --> 00:51:54.070
Come here.

00:51:54.070 --> 00:51:56.640
I'll comfort you and get
you into Heaven, you know?

00:51:56.640 --> 00:51:57.820
All the different things.

00:51:57.820 --> 00:52:01.770
Everything predicated on man
being in great pain, trouble.

00:52:01.770 --> 00:52:04.830
So then I realized that
rather big individuals who

00:52:04.830 --> 00:52:07.170
might be very excited
by anything you

00:52:07.170 --> 00:52:08.550
as the little
individual might do

00:52:08.550 --> 00:52:12.330
in way of finding a better
way of sun energy impounding--

00:52:12.330 --> 00:52:14.520
because it all
comes from the sun.

00:52:17.159 --> 00:52:19.200
They pay lip service to
you, but big government's

00:52:19.200 --> 00:52:21.410
going to do nothing about it.

00:52:21.410 --> 00:52:24.690
So I mean to say, what
are our odds here?

00:52:24.690 --> 00:52:27.580
Here we come to new knowledge,
first time in history,

00:52:27.580 --> 00:52:29.630
we don't have to be a failure.

00:52:29.630 --> 00:52:31.690
If we don't have
to be a failure,

00:52:31.690 --> 00:52:34.260
it doesn't have to be
you or me ever again.

00:52:34.260 --> 00:52:36.120
It doesn't have to be any war.

00:52:36.120 --> 00:52:38.256
You don't have to
rationalize selfishness.

00:52:38.256 --> 00:52:39.630
You don't have to
rationalize why

00:52:39.630 --> 00:52:41.460
your family is a
little more deserving

00:52:41.460 --> 00:52:42.751
than the other fellow's family.

00:52:42.751 --> 00:52:45.200
It's why you should
cheat the other guy.

00:52:45.200 --> 00:52:47.340
Just think if we get in
that kind of relationship

00:52:47.340 --> 00:52:48.460
to the universe.

00:52:48.460 --> 00:52:51.840
Anyway, I said that does not
seem to me to be unreasonable.

00:52:51.840 --> 00:52:53.770
But it does follow that
hydrogen atom doesn't

00:52:53.770 --> 00:52:55.030
have to earn a
living when it's not

00:52:55.030 --> 00:52:56.340
behaving like a hydrogen atom.

00:52:56.340 --> 00:52:58.750
In fact, the only
function that's

00:52:58.750 --> 00:53:02.220
come in the universe, that had
to do this you or me-ing, as

00:53:02.220 --> 00:53:03.650
far as I know, is human beings.

00:53:03.650 --> 00:53:05.150
There's all the
rest of the universe

00:53:05.150 --> 00:53:08.810
working very extraordinarily,
eternally regenerative.

00:53:08.810 --> 00:53:11.535
The only 100% efficient
system we know of.

00:53:11.535 --> 00:53:16.240
Now, this then brought
me to observing

00:53:16.240 --> 00:53:19.970
everything else I could,
and evolution is going on.

00:53:19.970 --> 00:53:22.040
I'll give a very big
evolutionary event.

00:53:25.580 --> 00:53:31.240
Historically, humans, like other
mammals, the female carrying

00:53:31.240 --> 00:53:33.400
the young, can't cover
as much geography

00:53:33.400 --> 00:53:35.140
annually as can the male.

00:53:35.140 --> 00:53:38.380
The North American wolf averages
a very much greater sweep out--

00:53:38.380 --> 00:53:40.820
the male does than the female.

00:53:40.820 --> 00:53:42.880
And so we have these in humans.

00:53:42.880 --> 00:53:48.460
The human female then
learned to get a fire going,

00:53:48.460 --> 00:53:52.780
and she could then keep the
food lasting a little longer.

00:53:52.780 --> 00:53:55.480
She learned how to dry it.

00:53:55.480 --> 00:53:58.130
She stayed around the hearth
preserving and consolidating

00:53:58.130 --> 00:53:58.630
the gains.

00:53:58.630 --> 00:54:00.150
The man was a hunter,
and he'd bring

00:54:00.150 --> 00:54:01.580
in a new kind of creature.

00:54:01.580 --> 00:54:05.020
She would decide whether
to skin it or milk it.

00:54:05.020 --> 00:54:08.040
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:54:08.040 --> 00:54:12.430
FULLER: And so gradually, the
man not only was the hunter,

00:54:12.430 --> 00:54:13.942
but he also was a newsbringer.

00:54:13.942 --> 00:54:16.400
Because he got to the top of
the mountain, and other people

00:54:16.400 --> 00:54:17.150
hadn't been there.

00:54:17.150 --> 00:54:21.760
So to all the children
through history, mom and dad

00:54:21.760 --> 00:54:24.110
were the authority on
what you can to eat--

00:54:24.110 --> 00:54:27.130
what their was that dad and mom
and found that you could eat,

00:54:27.130 --> 00:54:29.410
what the chieftain would
put up with, and so forth.

00:54:29.410 --> 00:54:33.040
Dad and mom were the authority
for this new little life here.

00:54:33.040 --> 00:54:38.222
Not only that, but dad in
addition was the newsman.

00:54:38.222 --> 00:54:40.780
And dad's language is very
inadequate and very poor

00:54:40.780 --> 00:54:44.220
over the great ages, but anyway.

00:54:44.220 --> 00:54:46.850
What he'd seen from the
top of the mountain,

00:54:46.850 --> 00:54:49.260
or he'd heard that
the chieftain said--

00:54:49.260 --> 00:54:50.770
and his language was very poor.

00:54:50.770 --> 00:54:53.310
But the kids, then--
dad is the authority,

00:54:53.310 --> 00:54:54.990
and this is the way dad says it.

00:54:54.990 --> 00:54:58.680
So the esoteric way of
communication went to the kids

00:54:58.680 --> 00:55:01.620
all right, but it started
more and more dialects

00:55:01.620 --> 00:55:03.550
and different languages.

00:55:03.550 --> 00:55:05.530
Suddenly, we have--

00:55:05.530 --> 00:55:08.245
I said the electron
coming in when I'm three.

00:55:08.245 --> 00:55:13.490
The year I was 23, we had
the human voice on the radio.

00:55:13.490 --> 00:55:17.290
The year I was 27, we had the
first licensed broadcasting

00:55:17.290 --> 00:55:19.000
radio station.

00:55:19.000 --> 00:55:23.080
In 1927, all the daddies
were coming home one evening,

00:55:23.080 --> 00:55:25.169
and all the kids said,
Daddy come in and listen

00:55:25.169 --> 00:55:25.710
to the radio.

00:55:25.710 --> 00:55:27.550
A man's flying
across the Atlantic.

00:55:27.550 --> 00:55:30.990
And Daddy never brought
the news home ever again.

00:55:30.990 --> 00:55:32.760
It stopped.

00:55:32.760 --> 00:55:36.110
Nobody thought about
this anthropologically.

00:55:36.110 --> 00:55:39.710
The news was it, and you're
preoccupied with the news.

00:55:39.710 --> 00:55:41.510
But the fact was,
then, the people

00:55:41.510 --> 00:55:44.000
who got the job on
the radio got it

00:55:44.000 --> 00:55:46.640
by virtue of the
commonality of their diction

00:55:46.640 --> 00:55:50.469
rather than special esoteric
way that Daddy said it.

00:55:50.469 --> 00:55:52.635
And they updated by virtue
of the size of vocabulary

00:55:52.635 --> 00:55:54.450
and they were skilled
in employing it.

00:55:54.450 --> 00:55:57.240
That's where they got their
jobs and then maintained them.

00:55:57.240 --> 00:55:59.970
And there's liquidity in
which they could get it out.

00:55:59.970 --> 00:56:04.474
So the kids then saw dad and
mom listening to that radio.

00:56:04.474 --> 00:56:06.390
And they saw dad run
across the street telling

00:56:06.390 --> 00:56:08.770
what the radio man said.

00:56:08.770 --> 00:56:11.885
So quite clearly, dad and
mom were the authority,

00:56:11.885 --> 00:56:13.260
but these were
more of authority,

00:56:13.260 --> 00:56:15.690
because dad and mom
are learning from them.

00:56:15.690 --> 00:56:18.360
So the kids then emulated
the words the way

00:56:18.360 --> 00:56:20.410
the great authority said it.

00:56:20.410 --> 00:56:23.582
This completely changed the
speech pattern of humanity.

00:56:23.582 --> 00:56:25.790
One of the things I've lived
through was that change.

00:56:25.790 --> 00:56:26.400
I'll show you.

00:56:26.400 --> 00:56:29.280
Here in Boston, my first
job before World War I,

00:56:29.280 --> 00:56:32.470
I worked with some
very expert craftsman,

00:56:32.470 --> 00:56:33.770
very fine human beings.

00:56:33.770 --> 00:56:35.080
They're very lovable.

00:56:35.080 --> 00:56:37.490
But their vocabulary
was about 100 words,

00:56:37.490 --> 00:56:39.270
50% blasphemous and obscene.

00:56:39.270 --> 00:56:40.869
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

00:56:40.869 --> 00:56:42.660
FULLER: Mainly the way
they spit to let you

00:56:42.660 --> 00:56:45.460
know how they feel about it.

00:56:45.460 --> 00:56:46.820
But this has really changed.

00:56:46.820 --> 00:56:48.360
It's incredible to me.

00:56:48.360 --> 00:56:51.710
I now have been around
the world 44 times,

00:56:51.710 --> 00:56:54.330
and the vocabulary around the
world is just extraordinary.

00:56:54.330 --> 00:56:57.420
I can really use the
very best I have in me,

00:56:57.420 --> 00:57:00.880
and I find myself being
understood very readily.

00:57:00.880 --> 00:57:03.120
Now, this all changed
in our lifetime,

00:57:03.120 --> 00:57:05.520
and it came about by
virtue of that radio

00:57:05.520 --> 00:57:09.000
and getting some commonality
of diction at some point.

00:57:09.000 --> 00:57:14.277
Now, the next thing that happens
is, nobody said to the kids,

00:57:14.277 --> 00:57:15.360
this is a great authority.

00:57:15.360 --> 00:57:19.790
It simply is self-evident that
this is the great authority.

00:57:19.790 --> 00:57:23.190
Now, the kids instinctively
follow the great authority.

00:57:23.190 --> 00:57:25.560
The child wants to know.

00:57:25.560 --> 00:57:29.580
So then, as you know,
the speed of sound

00:57:29.580 --> 00:57:31.635
approximately 700 miles an hour.

00:57:31.635 --> 00:57:34.541
The speed of light,
approximately 700 million miles

00:57:34.541 --> 00:57:35.040
an hour.

00:57:35.040 --> 00:57:36.900
Approximately a
million times faster.

00:57:36.900 --> 00:57:39.340
And sound only operates
in our atmosphere,

00:57:39.340 --> 00:57:41.840
and the light goes right on.

00:57:41.840 --> 00:57:44.830
The amount of information
you get visually

00:57:44.830 --> 00:57:49.450
in ratio to what you get through
your ears is a million-fold.

00:57:49.450 --> 00:57:53.410
So suddenly we have the
young students at Berkeley

00:57:53.410 --> 00:57:57.800
out in California making
the world news as dissenters

00:57:57.800 --> 00:58:00.624
about the educational system.

00:58:00.624 --> 00:58:03.040
That particular group asked
me to come and meet with them,

00:58:03.040 --> 00:58:06.490
and I met their contemporaries
at many universes out here.

00:58:06.490 --> 00:58:11.300
They graduated, and the majority
of them graduated in '66.

00:58:14.560 --> 00:58:16.760
Suddenly, I found
those kids were

00:58:16.760 --> 00:58:20.480
born the year the television
came in the American home.

00:58:20.480 --> 00:58:23.730
And they all said, I know that
dad and mom love me to pieces.

00:58:23.730 --> 00:58:25.410
I love dad and mom to pieces.

00:58:25.410 --> 00:58:26.910
But they don't know
what's going on,

00:58:26.910 --> 00:58:28.530
have the slightest
idea what was going on.

00:58:28.530 --> 00:58:30.780
They don't have anything to
do with our going to Korea

00:58:30.780 --> 00:58:32.030
or going to the moon.

00:58:32.030 --> 00:58:33.020
They don't have to
do with anything.

00:58:33.020 --> 00:58:34.436
They're just lovable
human beings,

00:58:34.436 --> 00:58:35.767
but the world is in trouble.

00:58:35.767 --> 00:58:38.100
And this information we're
getting from around the world

00:58:38.100 --> 00:58:39.710
now, not just locally anymore.

00:58:39.710 --> 00:58:42.374
Well, I guess, I had very local
information when I was young.

00:58:42.374 --> 00:58:43.790
They're really
getting world news.

00:58:43.790 --> 00:58:44.749
The world's in trouble.

00:58:44.749 --> 00:58:46.581
The older people don't
know what's going on.

00:58:46.581 --> 00:58:47.930
I've got to do my own thinking.

00:58:47.930 --> 00:58:50.210
Now, I'll show you
one of the things that

00:58:50.210 --> 00:58:51.890
was very different about this.

00:58:51.890 --> 00:58:53.349
When I was young--

00:58:53.349 --> 00:58:54.890
my father died when
I was very young.

00:58:54.890 --> 00:58:57.110
And my mother said, I'm
going to send you to the best

00:58:57.110 --> 00:58:58.212
school I can afford to do.

00:58:58.212 --> 00:58:59.420
I don't have very much money.

00:58:59.420 --> 00:59:00.800
We're going to want you--

00:59:00.800 --> 00:59:02.842
and she said, darling,
never mind what you think.

00:59:02.842 --> 00:59:03.341
Listen.

00:59:03.341 --> 00:59:04.510
We're trying to teach you.

00:59:04.510 --> 00:59:06.690
I went to school, and they
said, never mind what you think.

00:59:06.690 --> 00:59:08.315
This is what we're
trying to teach you.

00:59:08.315 --> 00:59:10.940
We're intended to only no
never mind what you think.

00:59:10.940 --> 00:59:13.880
I was also being told
by men as I got older

00:59:13.880 --> 00:59:15.000
that life was very tough.

00:59:15.000 --> 00:59:16.375
It had to be you
or me, so you've

00:59:16.375 --> 00:59:17.957
got to get over all
your sensitivity.

00:59:17.957 --> 00:59:20.290
Get over your sensitivity and
never mind what you think.

00:59:20.290 --> 00:59:23.325
So I found myself out
of the gate with it

00:59:23.325 --> 00:59:25.470
all So it was sort of a
game that you had to learn.

00:59:25.470 --> 00:59:28.457
And so I learned the
game as best I could.

00:59:28.457 --> 00:59:30.040
But nobody's saying
to the young world

00:59:30.040 --> 00:59:31.498
anymore, never mind
what you think.

00:59:31.498 --> 00:59:32.590
There's just none of it.

00:59:32.590 --> 00:59:35.690
We suddenly have a young world--

00:59:35.690 --> 00:59:38.090
that's just going back
then to the '60s--

00:59:38.090 --> 00:59:40.920
where suddenly a young world
started doing his own thinking.

00:59:40.920 --> 00:59:43.970
He's very knew at
that, very idealistic.

00:59:43.970 --> 00:59:47.540
With Russia and the United
States spending $200 million

00:59:47.540 --> 00:59:50.780
a year on how to destroy.

00:59:50.780 --> 00:59:53.850
They appropriate about $20
billion a year or 10% of it

00:59:53.850 --> 00:59:56.120
on how to break down
the other man's economy

00:59:56.120 --> 00:59:57.860
before you get to the war.

00:59:57.860 --> 00:59:58.500
And that's it.

00:59:58.500 --> 01:00:01.190
So the United States
had free press

01:00:01.190 --> 01:00:03.890
that was very much
easier to operate

01:00:03.890 --> 01:00:06.450
against than the
Russian side where

01:00:06.450 --> 01:00:07.717
they didn't have free press.

01:00:07.717 --> 01:00:10.300
I heard the Russians say-- they
said to me many times, I can't

01:00:10.300 --> 01:00:11.841
understand why you
keep a free press,

01:00:11.841 --> 01:00:14.635
because we can get a
bonfire going in America,

01:00:14.635 --> 01:00:15.830
it goes all over the place.

01:00:15.830 --> 01:00:18.770
At any rate, we
have then there was

01:00:18.770 --> 01:00:20.750
no question about
the young people who

01:00:20.750 --> 01:00:25.660
were very idealistic being
exploited very ingeniously.

01:00:25.660 --> 01:00:28.631
And so there were all kinds
of activism then in the '60s.

01:00:28.631 --> 01:00:31.130
But then suddenly the kids found
they were using their heads

01:00:31.130 --> 01:00:31.984
for battering rams.

01:00:31.984 --> 01:00:34.025
They said, I should use
my head for thinking, not

01:00:34.025 --> 01:00:34.858
for a battering ram.

01:00:34.858 --> 01:00:36.980
And so they began to
develop an immunization

01:00:36.980 --> 01:00:38.540
to the being exploitable.

01:00:38.540 --> 01:00:41.780
So today, they're
nowhere nearly.

01:00:41.780 --> 01:00:44.660
Each year, I'm finding
a very great difference.

01:00:44.660 --> 01:00:48.320
I have been a visitor
now at 550 university

01:00:48.320 --> 01:00:49.680
college around the world.

01:00:49.680 --> 01:00:51.054
Many of the colleges
many times--

01:00:51.054 --> 01:00:53.390
like MIT, in almost
innumerable times.

01:00:53.390 --> 01:00:56.240
I really have quite a
good feeling for you

01:00:56.240 --> 01:00:59.720
to tell you that there
is a very great strength

01:00:59.720 --> 01:01:02.660
in that young world today
doing its own thinking,

01:01:02.660 --> 01:01:05.030
and realizing it isn't
an invisible world.

01:01:05.030 --> 01:01:06.500
And you're going
to have then have

01:01:06.500 --> 01:01:09.030
competence to carry on
in the invisible world,

01:01:09.030 --> 01:01:11.270
the invisible reality.

01:01:11.270 --> 01:01:14.050
Which is what you have
here at MIT of all places.

01:01:14.050 --> 01:01:21.320
So the next thing I saw was each
child being born successively

01:01:21.320 --> 01:01:25.230
was being born in the presence
of less misinformation.

01:01:25.230 --> 01:01:26.980
And each new child
being born successfully

01:01:26.980 --> 01:01:30.660
being born in the presence of
much more reliable information.

01:01:30.660 --> 01:01:33.430
Now, I saw that--

01:01:33.430 --> 01:01:36.010
I'm getting letters
today, not so frequently,

01:01:36.010 --> 01:01:38.710
but I get them,
say, four or five

01:01:38.710 --> 01:01:40.960
a year from 8- and
10-year-olds who've been

01:01:40.960 --> 01:01:42.952
born after man got to the moon.

01:01:42.952 --> 01:01:45.160
And how they find that I'm
someone they can write to,

01:01:45.160 --> 01:01:46.243
I don't know, but they do.

01:01:46.243 --> 01:01:48.041
Their letters are
beautifully written.

01:01:48.041 --> 01:01:50.290
And they say, humanity can
do anything it needs to do.

01:01:50.290 --> 01:01:52.420
Why don't we make
this thing work?

01:01:52.420 --> 01:01:55.760
They're completely full
of concern about it.

01:01:55.760 --> 01:01:58.120
And I say, nature is coming
through with something new

01:01:58.120 --> 01:02:00.430
here in the way of capability.

01:02:00.430 --> 01:02:06.810
And so I have you also being
born naked, helpless, ignorant,

01:02:06.810 --> 01:02:08.840
having to learn by
trial and error.

01:02:08.840 --> 01:02:11.580
Humanity then gained the point
where it did develop words,

01:02:11.580 --> 01:02:13.380
did gain a whole
lot of information,

01:02:13.380 --> 01:02:16.315
but made an incredible number
of misinterpretation about--

01:02:16.315 --> 01:02:16.815
[AUDIO OUT]

01:02:16.815 --> 01:02:20.880
--you take a polished steel
ball 16 inches in diameter,

01:02:20.880 --> 01:02:23.850
it would probably be rougher
than our Earth's planet.

01:02:23.850 --> 01:02:26.310
Pictures taken of our planet
coming in from outer space,

01:02:26.310 --> 01:02:28.200
we can see through
the cloud cover.

01:02:28.200 --> 01:02:30.760
You can see the blue
water, the brown land,

01:02:30.760 --> 01:02:34.690
but you can't see mountains
let alone human beings.

01:02:34.690 --> 01:02:37.650
You and I standing on top of one
another's head making a chain,

01:02:37.650 --> 01:02:39.840
it'd take 10,000 of us
to make a difference

01:02:39.840 --> 01:02:42.270
between the outermost and
innermost points of our Earth.

01:02:42.270 --> 01:02:45.400
So you and I are
1/10,000 invisible.

01:02:45.400 --> 01:02:49.706
Now, our planet Earth's diameter
is about 1/100 that of the sun.

01:02:49.706 --> 01:02:51.450
If you look at the
sun in the afternoon

01:02:51.450 --> 01:02:53.820
when there's cloud in front
of his white does disc,

01:02:53.820 --> 01:02:56.771
take coins out of your pocket
at arm's length to try to cover

01:02:56.771 --> 01:02:57.270
it.

01:02:57.270 --> 01:02:59.070
A nickel just about covers it.

01:02:59.070 --> 01:03:04.260
You'll find that the size
of our Earth against that--

01:03:04.260 --> 01:03:06.190
our school rulers
remember, 1/16 of an inch.

01:03:06.190 --> 01:03:09.570
What, engineering scales get
down 1/50, 1/100 of an inch.

01:03:09.570 --> 01:03:11.880
But beyond there,
everything gets blurred.

01:03:11.880 --> 01:03:13.310
You have the very
finest printing

01:03:13.310 --> 01:03:16.080
where seeing absolute continuity
of red and the colors,

01:03:16.080 --> 01:03:17.670
you have 1/200 of an inch.

01:03:17.670 --> 01:03:21.650
Anyway, our planet Earth
is so small against the sun

01:03:21.650 --> 01:03:24.350
as you and I couldn't see
it, you couldn't see it.

01:03:24.350 --> 01:03:26.220
So you and I are
invisible on our planet,

01:03:26.220 --> 01:03:28.261
and our planet's invisible
against the sun, which

01:03:28.261 --> 01:03:29.830
