01:03:29.830 --> 01:03:32.240
We have 100 billion
stars in our galaxy.

01:03:32.240 --> 01:03:36.650
And let's look at Orion's
belt at two bright stars.

01:03:36.650 --> 01:03:39.321
One one of them,
Betelgeuse, its diameter

01:03:39.321 --> 01:03:41.570
is greater than the orbit
of the Earth around the sun.

01:03:41.570 --> 01:03:43.400
So there's a good
sized star, all right.

01:03:43.400 --> 01:03:46.293
But understand we have
a very small size where

01:03:46.293 --> 01:03:48.980
there are 100 billion
stars in our galaxy.

01:03:48.980 --> 01:03:53.300
We now know of 2
billion such galaxies.

01:03:53.300 --> 01:03:55.010
