01:08:21.620 --> 01:08:23.630
I'd like to be able to
take the data of a sphere

01:08:23.630 --> 01:08:25.399
and project it out on the flat.

01:08:25.399 --> 01:08:26.840
And I discover a
way of doing it.

01:08:26.840 --> 01:08:30.500
I'd like to tell you rather
quickly how it is completely

01:08:30.500 --> 01:08:32.450
unlike any of the
methods of projections

01:08:32.450 --> 01:08:34.189
that have been used.

01:08:34.189 --> 01:08:37.000
As we find mathematically,
you can divide--

01:08:37.000 --> 01:08:41.149
you can get three
triangles around a corner

01:08:41.149 --> 01:08:43.270
in a spherical tetrahedron.

01:08:43.270 --> 01:08:45.029
You can get four
equilateral triangles

01:08:45.029 --> 01:08:47.210
around an octohedron's corner.

01:08:47.210 --> 01:08:50.350
You can get five
icosahedron around a corner.

01:08:50.350 --> 01:08:54.210
You can't get six
because you have 60, 60,

01:08:54.210 --> 01:08:55.434
and you have 360 degrees.

01:08:55.434 --> 01:08:56.850
It'd be a plane
going to infinity,

01:08:56.850 --> 01:08:58.500
so in order to come
back in the south,

01:08:58.500 --> 01:09:00.291
the limited number of
equilateral triangles

01:09:00.291 --> 01:09:02.430
around a corner
can only be five.

01:09:02.430 --> 01:09:04.560
I took this
spherical icosahedron

01:09:04.560 --> 01:09:08.600
with its 20 equilateral
triangles-- each of the corners

01:09:08.600 --> 01:09:10.290
are 72 degrees.

01:09:10.290 --> 01:09:12.210
And I found a method then.

01:09:14.890 --> 01:09:17.590
If you think about
a steel band--

01:09:17.590 --> 01:09:22.540
three steel bands that
have inch marks on them,

01:09:22.540 --> 01:09:26.140
if I bend one of
them, the inch marks

01:09:26.140 --> 01:09:28.689
remain still an inch apart.

01:09:28.689 --> 01:09:34.370
If I then take three
such bands, and I

01:09:34.370 --> 01:09:38.899
am going to take each
of those bands and weld.

01:09:38.899 --> 01:09:40.850
Each one would be 12
inches long, the band.

01:09:40.850 --> 01:09:43.414
And I've got a
12-inch long rod going

01:09:43.414 --> 01:09:45.830
through each one at its point,
perpendicularly through it,

01:09:45.830 --> 01:09:49.180
welding it into place--
a very stiff carbon rod.

01:09:49.180 --> 01:09:52.470
And so it's 6 inches
above, 6 inches below.

01:09:52.470 --> 01:09:54.830
If I take those
ends of those rods

01:09:54.830 --> 01:09:57.020
and pull them together
with one steel band,

01:09:57.020 --> 01:09:58.360
the whole band will just bend.

01:09:58.360 --> 01:10:01.080
But the 1 inch points on
the band don't change.

01:10:01.080 --> 01:10:03.490
They hold a uniform
scale whether flat

01:10:03.490 --> 01:10:05.930
or in the band condition.

01:10:05.930 --> 01:10:12.980
If I take three
such steel rulers

01:10:12.980 --> 01:10:15.890
with three sets of
rods going through them

01:10:15.890 --> 01:10:22.250
as I spoke about it, and I
put a little bolt at the ends

01:10:22.250 --> 01:10:26.511
to make it into triangles, it
looks like a triangular fence.

01:10:26.511 --> 01:10:28.760
Now I'm going to take all
the bottom of all those rods

01:10:28.760 --> 01:10:29.718
and pull them together.

01:10:29.718 --> 01:10:34.220
It makes each of the bands bend,
but it makes two of the bands

01:10:34.220 --> 01:10:35.670
bend away from the third band.

01:10:35.670 --> 01:10:38.730
It opens up the
angle of the corner,

01:10:38.730 --> 01:10:40.830
makes sure it goes
spherical triangle.

01:10:40.830 --> 01:10:44.420
So it gets up to 72 degrees
and has to be, then, spherical.

01:10:44.420 --> 01:10:48.860
So with the icosahedron, I
have 20 spherical triangles.

01:10:48.860 --> 01:10:50.660
Each of those corners
is 72 degrees.

01:10:50.660 --> 01:10:54.710
When I take them off, holding
my uniform boundary scale

01:10:54.710 --> 01:10:57.590
so we don't let any infinity
in the system at all,

01:10:57.590 --> 01:11:01.090
then the corner angles
go from 72 to 60,

01:11:01.090 --> 01:11:03.920
which is called 12
degrees spherical excess.

01:11:03.920 --> 01:11:06.740
But because it's done absolute
symmetrically in equal angle

01:11:06.740 --> 01:11:10.139
triangles, then there's
shrinkage of the data

01:11:10.139 --> 01:11:11.930
inside the triangle
but not along the edge.

01:11:11.930 --> 01:11:13.960
The edge old absolutely true.

01:11:13.960 --> 01:11:16.240
There's a very mild
shrinkage internally,

01:11:16.240 --> 01:11:18.380
and it's mostly the center.

01:11:18.380 --> 01:11:22.130
And the shrinkage
is so minor, there's

01:11:22.130 --> 01:11:24.950
no visual distortion
between the relative shape

01:11:24.950 --> 01:11:29.090
and size of any of the parts
on the sphere or on the flaps.

