01:14:36.430 --> 01:14:39.790
of deep waterfront,
well-protected inside

01:14:39.790 --> 01:14:43.090
of the Long Island
and Staten Island.

01:14:43.090 --> 01:14:45.270
Then we have-- on
the West Coast,

01:14:45.270 --> 01:14:47.260
we had San Francisco, Seattle.

01:14:47.260 --> 01:14:51.190
There are relatively few
good harbors in the world.

01:14:51.190 --> 01:14:53.020
And North America,
then, would be

01:14:53.020 --> 01:14:55.990
able to build a railroad
between the East and West

01:14:55.990 --> 01:14:59.193
of the San Francisco and
the New York, and so forth.

01:14:59.193 --> 01:15:04.930
Now in 1961, three jet
airplanes which nobody knew

01:15:04.930 --> 01:15:08.225
were going to be coming,
three jet transport airplanes

01:15:08.225 --> 01:15:10.725
outperformed the Queen Mary,
Queen Elizabeth-- the steamship

01:15:10.725 --> 01:15:11.770
of the United States.

01:15:11.770 --> 01:15:15.010
In the year 1961, ships of
the sea became obsolete.

01:15:15.010 --> 01:15:19.130
Again, a big, big evolutionary
event for how humanity

01:15:19.130 --> 01:15:20.360
goes from here to there.

01:15:20.360 --> 01:15:21.734
From here on,
we're getting there

01:15:21.734 --> 01:15:24.240
by air, which was utterly
undreamed of in my mother's

01:15:24.240 --> 01:15:25.060
time.

01:15:25.060 --> 01:15:27.060
So we have, then--

01:15:27.060 --> 01:15:28.930
here's that great
water ocean world.

01:15:28.930 --> 01:15:30.820
And the British,
who were running it,

01:15:30.820 --> 01:15:34.690
then found if you got down
to the Southern Pacific here,

01:15:34.690 --> 01:15:37.360
you'd get on the
roaring force of how the

01:15:37.360 --> 01:15:40.060
what goes around west to east.

01:15:40.060 --> 01:15:42.967
The water went faster than
the crystalline Earth,

01:15:42.967 --> 01:15:44.300
and the winds even faster still.

01:15:44.300 --> 01:15:47.660
So we had what I call a Roaring
Forties going around here.

01:15:47.660 --> 01:15:49.730
There's no such
thing in the Arctic.

01:15:49.730 --> 01:15:51.100
But in the Antarctic, there is.

01:15:51.100 --> 01:15:54.520
And you can see where the great
ice floes chewed through what

01:15:54.520 --> 01:15:55.749
we call the Great Horn.

01:15:55.749 --> 01:15:57.540
So the British discovered
all you had to do

01:15:57.540 --> 01:15:59.957
was come south in the Pacific,
get in the Roaring Forties,

01:15:59.957 --> 01:16:01.414
you're going right
to the Atlantic.

01:16:01.414 --> 01:16:03.670
Come the south Atlantic,
ride on the Roaring Forties--

01:16:03.670 --> 01:16:04.760
in the Indian Ocean.

01:16:04.760 --> 01:16:07.420
Indian Ocean-- right
in the Pacific again.

01:16:07.420 --> 01:16:09.010
What do the British got?

01:16:09.010 --> 01:16:13.060
They got the southern tip of
South America, Africa, South

01:16:13.060 --> 01:16:15.159
Africa, Australia, New Zealand.

01:16:15.159 --> 01:16:16.450
They got on the merry-go-round.

01:16:16.450 --> 01:16:18.880
The people all the
way out here, no idea.

01:16:18.880 --> 01:16:22.090
So this is a picture
you're seeing first time

01:16:22.090 --> 01:16:23.890
the British Empire,
which they were not

01:16:23.890 --> 01:16:25.480
eager for anybody to see.

01:16:25.480 --> 01:16:26.790
Anywhere, there it is.

01:16:26.790 --> 01:16:30.700
And now 1961, those
airplanes they arrived sad.

01:16:30.700 --> 01:16:32.350
Next picture, please.

01:16:32.350 --> 01:16:33.670
Number two.

01:16:33.670 --> 01:16:38.840
So suddenly we have here what
I called a sky-ocean world.

01:16:38.840 --> 01:16:41.150
It's the first time
in your life or any--

01:16:41.150 --> 01:16:42.840
if you haven't seen
this map before,

01:16:42.840 --> 01:16:45.380
it's the first time
humanity is able to see

01:16:45.380 --> 01:16:49.180
all of the surface of our Earth
without any visible distortion

01:16:49.180 --> 01:16:52.350
of the relative shape or
size of any of the parts

01:16:52.350 --> 01:16:54.510
and without any break in
the continental contours.

01:16:54.510 --> 01:16:56.960
We have one world island
and one world ocean.

01:16:56.960 --> 01:16:58.940
It took me two years
to find out how to get

01:16:58.940 --> 01:17:00.890
all those sinuses in the water.

01:17:00.890 --> 01:17:02.180
But at any rate, there it is.

01:17:02.180 --> 01:17:04.864
So suddenly this is the
new intimacy-- this way.

01:17:04.864 --> 01:17:06.530
This is the way we're
going to be going.

01:17:06.530 --> 01:17:08.350
And we're still--

01:17:08.350 --> 01:17:10.460
I was just reading
this day's paper

01:17:10.460 --> 01:17:12.410
about New York getting
in a new convention

01:17:12.410 --> 01:17:15.080
center for $350 million.

01:17:15.080 --> 01:17:17.924
There's so much property in
New York and San Francisco

01:17:17.924 --> 01:17:20.090
that they'd do anything to
have conventions somehow,

01:17:20.090 --> 01:17:20.798
to keep it going.

01:17:20.798 --> 01:17:24.640
But absolutely dead--
obsolete, utterly obsolete.

01:17:24.640 --> 01:17:28.390
We have then, when I was
young, 90% of Americans

01:17:28.390 --> 01:17:31.005
were on farms-- today, only 7%.

01:17:31.005 --> 01:17:33.380
And all the people that started
for a moment hanging fire

01:17:33.380 --> 01:17:34.460
are using those cities.

01:17:34.460 --> 01:17:37.440
There are dormitories, the
sort of big university areas,

01:17:37.440 --> 01:17:41.000
but they're obsolete as
anything to do with the way they

01:17:41.000 --> 01:17:42.960
were conceived originally.

01:17:42.960 --> 01:17:47.440
And now on this map,
you'll find humanity.

01:17:47.440 --> 01:17:50.870
And I find that it is--

01:17:50.870 --> 01:17:53.677
95% of humanity can reach
each other on the shortest

01:17:53.677 --> 01:17:56.010
great circle air routes without
going near the Atlantic,

01:17:56.010 --> 01:17:58.060
Pacific, or Indian Ocean.

01:17:58.060 --> 01:18:01.050
So this is a north-south world.

01:18:01.050 --> 01:18:02.955
And I found something
else very fascinating.

01:18:02.955 --> 01:18:04.770
It's coming in with the--

01:18:04.770 --> 01:18:08.510
you may remember that the
delivery of electricity,

01:18:08.510 --> 01:18:10.520
delivery of energy
from here there,

01:18:10.520 --> 01:18:14.820
there's no way we get so
much so fast as by wire.

01:18:14.820 --> 01:18:19.650
And the limit of the practical
deliverability from World War I

01:18:19.650 --> 01:18:22.940
on up to recently was
only 350 miles when

01:18:22.940 --> 01:18:25.160
you go across the time zones.

01:18:25.160 --> 01:18:27.630
But since the space
program came in

01:18:27.630 --> 01:18:30.480
and got what it called
ultra high voltage,

01:18:30.480 --> 01:18:33.640
we have Americans now
deliver 1,500 miles.

01:18:33.640 --> 01:18:37.980
I made a world network of
electrical energy networks

01:18:37.980 --> 01:18:41.670
not only then showing how we
then go across our time zones.

01:18:41.670 --> 01:18:44.460
And anyway, those times
zones would reach very nicely

01:18:44.460 --> 01:18:46.120
from here to Alaska.

01:18:46.120 --> 01:18:49.110
And in Alaska, we can
reach right across.

01:18:49.110 --> 01:18:53.330
The Russians have been building
hydraulic electric stations

01:18:53.330 --> 01:18:55.830
along all their
northern-flowing rivers in here.

01:18:55.830 --> 01:18:58.496
1,500 miles, you can reach
across to the Russian network.

01:18:58.496 --> 01:19:00.870
And that means you can get
into the China network and all

01:19:00.870 --> 01:19:02.100
the rest of the world.

01:19:02.100 --> 01:19:09.580
Now, when Trudeau was about to
make his first trip to Russia--

01:19:09.580 --> 01:19:13.430
we are friends, and I showed
him my electrical energy network

01:19:13.430 --> 01:19:14.030
grid.

01:19:14.030 --> 01:19:15.155
And he was very excited by it.

01:19:15.155 --> 01:19:15.750
So he took it.

01:19:15.750 --> 01:19:18.030
He gave it to Breshinev,
and Breshinev had

01:19:18.030 --> 01:19:19.280
his technical people check in.

01:19:19.280 --> 01:19:22.800
They said it looked very,
very practical to them.

01:19:22.800 --> 01:19:26.340
I can simply say to you with
all the nonsense going on

01:19:26.340 --> 01:19:28.040
in our world--

01:19:28.040 --> 01:19:30.350
money world today--
we've completely

01:19:30.350 --> 01:19:32.260
separated money from wealth.

01:19:32.260 --> 01:19:34.970
Wealth being the ability
to take care of human life.

01:19:34.970 --> 01:19:37.719
We have, as I just gave
you a little while ago,

01:19:37.719 --> 01:19:39.260
the ability to take
care of everybody

01:19:39.260 --> 01:19:40.460
at the highest
standard as others.

01:19:40.460 --> 01:19:42.440
We have 4 billion
billionaires on the planet

01:19:42.440 --> 01:19:43.100
right now, by the way.

01:19:43.100 --> 01:19:45.650
The game of money being played
keeps everything very scarce

01:19:45.650 --> 01:19:46.390
again.

01:19:46.390 --> 01:19:49.870
So the money game is going
to go out completely.

01:19:49.870 --> 01:19:51.110
We're going to be a mess.

01:19:51.110 --> 01:19:53.970
And what will happen is
we'll all get onto the--

01:19:53.970 --> 01:19:56.320
what it the accounting
system of the universe?

01:19:56.320 --> 01:19:57.270
It's energy.

01:19:57.270 --> 01:19:59.160
And energy and time.

01:19:59.160 --> 01:20:01.480
Energy and time--
and nothing else.

01:20:01.480 --> 01:20:03.680
And so we're going to
get on energy time.

01:20:03.680 --> 01:20:05.380
So the minute we get
on the same grid,

01:20:05.380 --> 01:20:11.090
it's going to be very, very easy
to really have the vaccinating

01:20:11.090 --> 01:20:12.349
or whatever we need to do.

01:20:12.349 --> 01:20:14.390
Way of accounting can be
done this way absolutely

01:20:14.390 --> 01:20:15.110
beautifully.

01:20:15.110 --> 01:20:18.490
So I want to give you a
few little quick insights.

01:20:18.490 --> 01:20:20.465
Now, that is all I'm
going to show you

01:20:20.465 --> 01:20:21.000
in the way of pictures.

01:20:21.000 --> 01:20:22.010
All I wanted to do was--

01:20:22.010 --> 01:20:23.350
may we have the lights on?

01:20:23.350 --> 01:20:27.110
I mainly just wanted to give you
a sense of very swift-- oh, no.

01:20:27.110 --> 01:20:28.380
One-- whoa, whoa stop.

01:20:28.380 --> 01:20:32.780
One more, one more,
one more, one more.

01:20:32.780 --> 01:20:34.180
All right.

01:20:34.180 --> 01:20:35.660
Sharpen it up best you can.

01:20:39.780 --> 01:20:42.270
Now, people you won't to
be able to read this chart,

01:20:42.270 --> 01:20:44.550
so I'll just simply tell
you what it's all about.

01:20:44.550 --> 01:20:48.390
It is a chart that
is 800 years long.

01:20:48.390 --> 01:20:57.160
And-- am I in your
way too much here?

01:20:57.160 --> 01:21:00.520
This chart-- I wanted
to have, as I call it,

01:21:00.520 --> 01:21:06.880
a way of charting gains
of science against time.

01:21:06.880 --> 01:21:09.460
Within science, of course,
we have then, as you say,

01:21:09.460 --> 01:21:10.140
pure science.

01:21:10.140 --> 01:21:12.820
And then within pure science,
we have the isolating

01:21:12.820 --> 01:21:14.585
of the chemical elements.

01:21:14.585 --> 01:21:16.210
And the isolating
the chemical elements

01:21:16.210 --> 01:21:18.800
happens to be a
closed system affair

01:21:18.800 --> 01:21:21.990
where membership is absolute
and right by the number.

01:21:21.990 --> 01:21:23.940
And that's all the
numbers have to be filled.

01:21:23.940 --> 01:21:26.650
We have one electron, one
photon, et cetera, et cetera.

01:21:26.650 --> 01:21:29.090
Nobody can cheat, at any rate.

01:21:29.090 --> 01:21:34.930
We have, when history opens,
humanity had already discovered

01:21:34.930 --> 01:21:36.640
and was using the--

01:21:40.920 --> 01:21:45.110
we have carbon lead, tin,
mercury, silver, copper,

01:21:45.110 --> 01:21:47.470
sulfur, gold, and iron.

01:21:47.470 --> 01:21:50.620
On this chart, I go up
one step every time we've

01:21:50.620 --> 01:21:52.000
isolated a chemical element.

01:21:52.000 --> 01:21:56.136
So it starts nine steps high.

01:21:56.136 --> 01:22:00.490
It's 1200 AD is the first known
isolation of a chemical element

01:22:00.490 --> 01:22:01.570
by a human being--

01:22:01.570 --> 01:22:02.560
arsenic.

01:22:02.560 --> 01:22:04.300
That's where my chart starts.

01:22:04.300 --> 01:22:08.200
We go 200 years, then
we come to antimony.

01:22:08.200 --> 01:22:10.060
200 years more, then phosphorus.

01:22:10.060 --> 01:22:13.540
Then 75 years, and it suddenly
starts climbing very rapidly.

01:22:13.540 --> 01:22:16.540
You see an accelerating
time and a slow down time--

01:22:16.540 --> 01:22:18.160
accelerating, a slow down.

01:22:18.160 --> 01:22:20.470
The accelerations
are always peacetime.

01:22:20.470 --> 01:22:23.050
These slowdowns
are always wartime.

01:22:23.050 --> 01:22:27.010
Now, we get to a point where--
and I'll get the pointer again.

01:22:27.010 --> 01:22:36.310
And suddenly this very much
was flattening out here.

01:22:36.310 --> 01:22:40.440
This is 1932, so the
depth of the Depression,

01:22:40.440 --> 01:22:42.120
but also the year
in which we made

01:22:42.120 --> 01:22:47.190
the 91st isolation of chemical
element only 90 out of 92--

01:22:47.190 --> 01:22:50.370
91 only present on the
planet, so we could isolate.

01:22:50.370 --> 01:22:53.090
Any rate, we have
here the, the shelves

01:22:53.090 --> 01:22:55.210
have fallen for the
first time in history.

01:22:55.210 --> 01:22:57.000
We've taken the
physical universe

01:22:57.000 --> 01:22:59.700
apart into its own
unique chemical elements

01:22:59.700 --> 01:23:02.850
to be reassociated
into preferable ways.

01:23:02.850 --> 01:23:05.160
From there on, we get
into post-uranium,

01:23:05.160 --> 01:23:07.290
and then suddenly
it's going like this.

01:23:07.290 --> 01:23:09.994
Now, very interesting,
they come in here.

01:23:09.994 --> 01:23:12.160
They don't come in by the
number of chemical number.

01:23:12.160 --> 01:23:15.780
37 might be the seventeenth
isolation, and so forth.

01:23:15.780 --> 01:23:17.820
But from here on,
they're coming in exactly

01:23:17.820 --> 01:23:20.310
by the numbers, which is a
very extraordinary thing.

01:23:20.310 --> 01:23:23.910
Any rate, against this
background of pure science,

01:23:23.910 --> 01:23:26.420
we have, then, applied
science, obviously.

01:23:26.420 --> 01:23:31.080
And what does humanity try to
do with this type of capability?

01:23:31.080 --> 01:23:33.360
It tries to clothe--

01:23:33.360 --> 01:23:34.804
it starts naked, yes?

01:23:34.804 --> 01:23:36.220
And then it gets
some skins on it,

01:23:36.220 --> 01:23:38.730
so it gets ready
to get in the cold.

01:23:38.730 --> 01:23:40.500
Then you put a double
skin in a tent,

01:23:40.500 --> 01:23:43.470
and get ready for colder still.

01:23:43.470 --> 01:23:45.660
Against this
background of science,

01:23:45.660 --> 01:23:49.650
I give humanity the requirement
to develop an environment

01:23:49.650 --> 01:23:51.400
control device.

01:23:51.400 --> 01:23:54.420
Which you can get into,
and from inside of it,

01:23:54.420 --> 01:23:56.790
control the energies
operating outside

01:23:56.790 --> 01:23:59.860
to take him in one complete
circuit of our planet.

01:23:59.860 --> 01:24:02.310
But we're going to have an
absolutely standard performance

01:24:02.310 --> 01:24:04.710
requirement against
his background.

01:24:04.710 --> 01:24:07.080
Here he goes around
in a wooden sailing

01:24:07.080 --> 01:24:09.550
ship for the first time.

01:24:09.550 --> 01:24:13.730
350 years later, he goes
around in a steel steamship.

01:24:13.730 --> 01:24:17.290
75 years later, goes around
in an aluminum airplane.

01:24:17.290 --> 01:24:21.530
35 years later, he goes around
in an exotic metal rocket.

01:24:21.530 --> 01:24:23.330
At the time when this
wooden sailing ship,

01:24:23.330 --> 01:24:26.200
nobody could dream of the
possibility of a steel

01:24:26.200 --> 01:24:27.000
steamship.

01:24:27.000 --> 01:24:29.120
At the of the steel
steamship, nobody

01:24:29.120 --> 01:24:31.130
could dream of an aluminum
airplane, let alone

01:24:31.130 --> 01:24:33.630
we hadn't learned to fly yet.

01:24:33.630 --> 01:24:36.390
Time of the airplane, nobody
could dream of an exotic metal

01:24:36.390 --> 01:24:37.850
rocket.

01:24:37.850 --> 01:24:41.200
So yes, having some enormous
acceleration going on here.

01:24:41.200 --> 01:24:44.250
You have this basic acceleration
of science against time.

01:24:44.250 --> 01:24:48.860
We have a contraction of 350
years, 75 years, 35 years.

01:24:48.860 --> 01:24:51.000
This one took two
years to go around.

01:24:51.000 --> 01:24:52.640
This one took two
months to go around.

01:24:52.640 --> 01:24:54.015
This took two
weeks to go around.

01:24:54.015 --> 01:24:56.500
This one took a
little over one hour.

01:24:56.500 --> 01:24:59.120
You're witnessing
quite visibly three--

01:24:59.120 --> 01:25:01.550
third power acceleration.

01:25:01.550 --> 01:25:03.080
It's implicit on this chart.

01:25:03.080 --> 01:25:06.470
If we go to 1985,
right in here, I'm

01:25:06.470 --> 01:25:08.180
going to have to send
you around in a way

01:25:08.180 --> 01:25:10.010
inconceivable in the
time of the exotic--

01:25:10.010 --> 01:25:12.344
I'm going to have to
send you around by radio.

01:25:12.344 --> 01:25:13.220
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:25:13.220 --> 01:25:15.580
FULLER: This chart is
the most powerful thing

01:25:15.580 --> 01:25:18.070
I've ever had to get
me to really feel--

01:25:18.070 --> 01:25:20.784
want you to feel-- the
acceleration that we're in.

01:25:20.784 --> 01:25:22.200
Because all of the
things that you

01:25:22.200 --> 01:25:24.910
have been very familiar with,
like the nations are going

01:25:24.910 --> 01:25:27.130
to go, and you
see, in this case,

01:25:27.130 --> 01:25:30.130
the United States going into
bankruptcy, going into--

01:25:30.130 --> 01:25:32.830
all these great power really
going downhill very rapidly.

01:25:32.830 --> 01:25:35.280
You're going to have all
kinds of things coming apart

01:25:35.280 --> 01:25:36.910
that you've been
very familiar with.

01:25:36.910 --> 01:25:38.410
And in its place,
you're going to be

01:25:38.410 --> 01:25:41.610
coming at some of the things
I've been talking to you about.

01:25:41.610 --> 01:25:43.380
I've taken lot of your time.

01:25:43.380 --> 01:25:47.590
Let me see what we are at
in the way of the clock.

01:25:47.590 --> 01:25:50.230
That is the end of slides.

01:25:50.230 --> 01:25:53.180
You can put on the
lights again now.

01:25:53.180 --> 01:25:55.640
It is now 9:30.

01:25:55.640 --> 01:25:59.390
I've been exactly the hour and
a half that we're supposed to.

01:25:59.390 --> 01:26:01.460
Now we're supposed to
get into questions.

01:26:01.460 --> 01:26:04.700
You have a choice of asking
me questions or letting

01:26:04.700 --> 01:26:06.850
me ask myself the questions
I've been asking myself

01:26:06.850 --> 01:26:08.671
for a very long time
and answering them

01:26:08.671 --> 01:26:09.965
in some kind of order for you.

01:26:09.965 --> 01:26:10.935
