justify the strange hour.

01:26:28.920 --> 01:26:29.842
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:26:29.842 --> 01:26:31.050
FULLER: I say, do I know you?

01:26:31.050 --> 01:26:31.740
And they say, no.

01:26:31.740 --> 01:26:34.115
And I say, I've got a very
important question to ask you.

01:26:34.115 --> 01:26:35.054
I said, all right.

01:26:35.054 --> 01:26:36.970
I assume then you must
think I have an answer.

01:26:36.970 --> 01:26:38.790
That's why you're calling.

01:26:38.790 --> 01:26:42.540
I do have an answer because 52
years ago, I made up my mind.

01:26:42.540 --> 01:26:44.550
I'm not going to ask
anybody else any question.

01:26:44.550 --> 01:26:45.925
I'm going to find
out for myself.

01:26:45.925 --> 01:26:48.859
So if you really want me to
help you, I suggest you hang up.

01:26:48.859 --> 01:26:49.400
And I listen.

01:26:49.400 --> 01:26:51.854
I listen, and granted, I say,
a few of them do hang up.

01:26:51.854 --> 01:26:53.520
But they start their
talking, and then I

01:26:53.520 --> 01:26:56.512
know they're just lonely,
call up to show off.

01:26:56.512 --> 01:26:57.503
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:26:57.503 --> 01:26:59.539
FULLER: So I hang up.

01:26:59.539 --> 01:27:01.535
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:27:01.535 --> 01:27:04.530
[APPLAUSE]

01:27:04.530 --> 01:27:06.320
FULLER: Anyway, I
would like to give you

01:27:06.320 --> 01:27:09.420
a little bit of what I think
of some of the things that--

01:27:09.420 --> 01:27:13.880
you're going to not only see
all the great nations going

01:27:13.880 --> 01:27:14.390
and going.

01:27:14.390 --> 01:27:17.180
They'll have to
go with 10 years.

01:27:17.180 --> 01:27:19.290
I feel that to--

01:27:19.290 --> 01:27:20.390
to have a very--

01:27:20.390 --> 01:27:22.056
I'm going to carry
through a little more

01:27:22.056 --> 01:27:25.760
on the function of humans in
universe, which I spoke about

01:27:25.760 --> 01:27:28.234
as having a mind capability.

01:27:35.630 --> 01:27:38.930
I said, what can I find
that's common to all lives

01:27:38.930 --> 01:27:41.630
in all history right up
to this minute, second?

01:27:41.630 --> 01:27:45.200
That is, common to all lives
are problem, problems, problems.

01:27:45.200 --> 01:27:47.962
That all of us here are
for problem solving.

01:27:47.962 --> 01:27:49.670
And if we're any good
at problem solving,

01:27:49.670 --> 01:27:51.586
you get much more difficult
problems to solve.

01:27:51.586 --> 01:27:53.030
It don't come to utopia at all.

01:27:53.030 --> 01:27:55.030
It was exactly the
opposite direction.

01:27:55.030 --> 01:27:57.632
That we're quite here
for problem solving,

01:27:57.632 --> 01:27:59.090
and we've been
given access to some

01:27:59.090 --> 01:28:02.780
of the great design of universe
to help us solve the problems.

01:28:02.780 --> 01:28:07.100
I say, let's you and I look at a
great design like a Boeing 747,

01:28:07.100 --> 01:28:09.010
go up inside of all
these instruments.

01:28:09.010 --> 01:28:11.134
And all those
instruments are connected

01:28:11.134 --> 01:28:12.550
with different
parts of your ship,

01:28:12.550 --> 01:28:15.530
and the power plant,
and the airframe.

01:28:15.530 --> 01:28:18.140
Every bit of critical
information regarding that ship

01:28:18.140 --> 01:28:19.299
is coming to you.

01:28:19.299 --> 01:28:20.840
And this is inherently
just to people

01:28:20.840 --> 01:28:23.630
who don't get into technology
to think about what's

01:28:23.630 --> 01:28:24.920
really going on here.

01:28:24.920 --> 01:28:28.570
In designing a single
family residence,

01:28:28.570 --> 01:28:30.800
500 drawings is the
most you have to have.

01:28:30.800 --> 01:28:34.340
You may use 1,000 of this
type of nail, but 500 will do.

01:28:34.340 --> 01:28:37.970
And the tolerance--
1/16 of an inch is fine.

01:28:37.970 --> 01:28:40.010
Get into the automobile
which is moving around

01:28:40.010 --> 01:28:41.720
in different parts
at different rates.

01:28:41.720 --> 01:28:43.390
We have to really
look out for that.

01:28:43.390 --> 01:28:46.940
We get to 5,000 types of parts
in an automobile and tolerances

01:28:46.940 --> 01:28:48.770
of 1/10,000 of an inch.

01:28:48.770 --> 01:28:52.430
We're getting that Boeing 747,
we're up to about 50,000 types

01:28:52.430 --> 01:28:54.640
of parts with tolerances
sometimes 1/1,000,000

01:28:54.640 --> 01:28:56.090
of an inch.

01:28:56.090 --> 01:28:59.350
There's more engineering goes
in one rivet in a Boeing 747

01:28:59.350 --> 01:29:01.280
than a whole single
family dwelling or even

01:29:01.280 --> 01:29:02.230
the automobile.

01:29:04.900 --> 01:29:09.480
And then that beautiful
thing in the sky,

01:29:09.480 --> 01:29:13.440
it has to be able to
take 650 miles an hour,

01:29:13.440 --> 01:29:16.780
which is 10 times the
velocity of a hurricane.

01:29:16.780 --> 01:29:22.570
And the resistance increases
second power of the speed

01:29:22.570 --> 01:29:26.160
so that the ferocity of the
interaction of the Boeing

01:29:26.160 --> 01:29:31.610
747 with atmosphere is 100 times
the ferocity of a hurricane.

01:29:31.610 --> 01:29:34.060
There's no way for our
imagination to really--

01:29:34.060 --> 01:29:36.476
and there's that thing going
around the silver thing going

01:29:36.476 --> 01:29:37.200
like that.

01:29:37.200 --> 01:29:41.950
You take 350 tons and land
it at 150 miles an hour.

01:29:41.950 --> 01:29:43.940
The music going is
quite a piece of design.

01:29:43.940 --> 01:29:48.490
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:29:48.490 --> 01:29:51.100
FULLER: When they say, better
fasten your seat belts,

01:29:51.100 --> 01:29:56.330
it's bumpy today, the stress
involved with that ship is

01:29:56.330 --> 01:29:58.810
the equivalent to taking
Queen Mary over Niagara Falls

01:29:58.810 --> 01:30:00.160
and saying its' bumpy today.

01:30:00.160 --> 01:30:02.160
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:30:02.160 --> 01:30:04.970
FULLER: It's an incredible
piece of design.

01:30:04.970 --> 01:30:06.950
And humanity knows
so little of this.

01:30:06.950 --> 01:30:10.100
The ignorance of
humanity because of what

01:30:10.100 --> 01:30:17.920
I've said of the invisibility
of the reality is, as I said--

01:30:17.920 --> 01:30:22.790
today, there are 40 million
engineers and scientists

01:30:22.790 --> 01:30:26.680
on our planet, but that's
only 1% of humanity.

01:30:26.680 --> 01:30:30.360
And the 99% don't
understand science

01:30:30.360 --> 01:30:33.210
because they don't understand
the language of science.

01:30:33.210 --> 01:30:35.610
And the 99% who don't understand
the language of science,

01:30:35.610 --> 01:30:38.404
and words being
quite new to them,

01:30:38.404 --> 01:30:40.320
think of the word
technology as something new.

01:30:40.320 --> 01:30:42.550
They don't know that all
the science we've ever found

01:30:42.550 --> 01:30:46.690
is the universe's most
incredible technology.

01:30:46.690 --> 01:30:50.320
So the 99% think of
technology as something new--

01:30:50.320 --> 01:30:53.174
as weaponry and machinery
to compete for their jobs.

01:30:53.174 --> 01:30:54.590
And they think
they're against it.

01:30:54.590 --> 01:30:57.670
So here we have humanity
as only out to really make

01:30:57.670 --> 01:31:02.020
it is by a design revolution,
using technology to really make

01:31:02.020 --> 01:31:04.720
humanity a success, to be
proud of the great success

01:31:04.720 --> 01:31:06.070
of the universe itself.

01:31:06.070 --> 01:31:09.455
So that's really
a very tough one.

01:31:09.455 --> 01:31:16.410
And that relates primarily to
the fact that the mathematics

01:31:16.410 --> 01:31:18.480
is a blockage--

01:31:18.480 --> 01:31:23.780
where it's indigestible
to leave many.

01:31:23.780 --> 01:31:26.560
I'd like to get that point
out of the way in a hurry.

01:31:26.560 --> 01:31:31.090
I became convinced when I
was very young the nature was

01:31:31.090 --> 01:31:35.380
coordinating in a way that
was not best expressed

01:31:35.380 --> 01:31:38.560
by the mathematics
I was being taught.

01:31:38.560 --> 01:31:41.159
I've been taught, for
instance, about pi--

01:31:41.159 --> 01:31:42.950
that you couldn't design
a circle or sphere

01:31:42.950 --> 01:31:44.345
without using pi.

01:31:44.345 --> 01:31:46.700
And I was taught, as I
stayed in mathematics,

01:31:46.700 --> 01:31:49.085
that pi was what is called
transcendental irrational.

01:31:49.085 --> 01:31:51.480
It could never be resolved.

01:31:51.480 --> 01:31:53.320
So I said, every time
nature makes a bubble,

01:31:53.320 --> 01:31:55.140
how many times does
she carry out pi

01:31:55.140 --> 01:31:56.970
before she discovers
it can't be resolved?

01:31:56.970 --> 01:32:00.150
What time does nature decide
to make a fake bubble?

01:32:00.150 --> 01:32:03.340
I don't think
nature is using pi.

01:32:03.340 --> 01:32:05.430
I don't think nature has
a departments of physics,

01:32:05.430 --> 01:32:07.697
and mathematics,
and biology, and has

01:32:07.697 --> 01:32:09.780
to have department head
meeting to know what to do

01:32:09.780 --> 01:32:11.570
when a leaf falls in the water.

01:32:11.570 --> 01:32:15.910
She has only one department, and
I'm eager to find it if I can.

01:32:15.910 --> 01:32:19.380
And I found nature never
saying, what shall I do?

01:32:27.468 --> 01:32:29.405
I don't have to make--

01:32:29.405 --> 01:32:31.030
nature knew I wouldn't
know what to do.

01:32:31.030 --> 01:32:33.014
And nature knew
exactly what to do.

01:32:33.014 --> 01:32:36.732
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:32:36.732 --> 01:32:38.190
FULLER: So I said,
I'd like to find

01:32:38.190 --> 01:32:40.100
nature's coordinate system.

01:32:40.100 --> 01:32:42.760
And I don't think it's
going to be x, y, z,

01:32:42.760 --> 01:32:45.420
flat, perpendicular. world
because that was when

01:32:45.420 --> 01:32:47.020
we thought of the flat Earth.

01:32:47.020 --> 01:32:49.810
So that would have been very
convenient if it was true.

01:32:49.810 --> 01:32:57.149
And I said, I made myself a
tubular necklace of four tubes,

01:32:57.149 --> 01:32:58.690
and I found it didn't
hold its shape.

01:32:58.690 --> 01:33:00.760
So I don't think she's
using a square either,

01:33:00.760 --> 01:33:04.120
because it there's no such
thing that won't hold its shape.

01:33:04.120 --> 01:33:06.550
I think nature-- if I want to
get anywhere near what she's

01:33:06.550 --> 01:33:08.760
doing, I'm going to
have to deal in her

01:33:08.760 --> 01:33:11.855
in the terms of right from the
beginning with all the energy

01:33:11.855 --> 01:33:12.355
qualities.

01:33:12.355 --> 01:33:14.050
It has to have heat.

01:33:14.050 --> 01:33:16.060
It has to have longevity.

01:33:16.060 --> 01:33:17.980
It has to have weight.

01:33:17.980 --> 01:33:20.017
And I saw the centimeter,
grams, seconds systems

01:33:20.017 --> 01:33:21.100
tried very hard to get it.

01:33:21.100 --> 01:33:24.010
But they never could
get the temperature in.

01:33:24.010 --> 01:33:28.242
So I said, well, I'm
going to deal in vectors.

01:33:28.242 --> 01:33:29.950
I like vectors, and
I learned about those

01:33:29.950 --> 01:33:30.847
at the Naval Academy.

01:33:30.847 --> 01:33:33.430
I'd been taught about a straight
line by my teacher at school.

01:33:33.430 --> 01:33:35.061
She said, there's
a straight line.

01:33:35.061 --> 01:33:36.810
I said it didn't look
very straight to me.

01:33:36.810 --> 01:33:38.176
But she said it was.

01:33:38.176 --> 01:33:39.550
And she said it
went to infinity.

01:33:39.550 --> 01:33:40.920
And I said, where's
the other gone?

01:33:40.920 --> 01:33:41.753
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:33:41.753 --> 01:33:43.362
FULLER: And she
couldn't tell me.

01:33:43.362 --> 01:33:45.820
So I didn't like the kinds of
things being taught at school

01:33:45.820 --> 01:33:47.320
at all.

01:33:47.320 --> 01:33:49.850
And I finally then
got into pursuing

01:33:49.850 --> 01:33:51.130
nature's own coordinates.

01:33:51.130 --> 01:33:55.060
And I'll point out to you
that nature does not operate

01:33:55.060 --> 01:33:57.070
perpendicularly parallel.

01:33:57.070 --> 01:33:59.220
Nature is convergent
And divergent.

01:33:59.220 --> 01:34:02.732
She is radiation, divergent,
gravitation, convergent--

01:34:02.732 --> 01:34:04.190
everything that
experience says has

01:34:04.190 --> 01:34:06.940
to do with waves going
omnidirectionally.

01:34:06.940 --> 01:34:09.490
So I've discovered nature's
own coordinate system.

01:34:09.490 --> 01:34:12.100
It turns out to be a
nominally triangulating world

01:34:12.100 --> 01:34:15.970
where the minimum smallest
system in universe

01:34:15.970 --> 01:34:16.930
is a tetrahedron.

01:34:16.930 --> 01:34:21.370
The minimum-- the only polygon
that is self-stabilizing

01:34:21.370 --> 01:34:22.460
is a triangle.

01:34:22.460 --> 01:34:26.890
And that is-- the tetrahedron
is the smallest, simplest

01:34:26.890 --> 01:34:28.800
structural system in
the universe so far.

01:34:28.800 --> 01:34:29.675
We've gone into this.

01:34:29.675 --> 01:34:32.250
And you can read my book,
Synergetics, at any rate.

01:34:32.250 --> 01:34:35.170
And another book-- volume
two-- will be coming out

01:34:35.170 --> 01:34:37.120
in September of this year.

01:34:37.120 --> 01:34:39.250
And it's very much
more voluminous.

01:34:39.250 --> 01:34:42.165
And we're absolutely
confident now we really

01:34:42.165 --> 01:34:45.170
have found nature's coordinate
system-- entirely rational.

01:34:45.170 --> 01:34:47.530
It's entirely conceptual,
and any little child

01:34:47.530 --> 01:34:49.130
could really understand it.

01:34:49.130 --> 01:34:51.387
And enough about that.

01:34:51.387 --> 01:34:53.220
But I think it's going
to be possible, then,

01:34:53.220 --> 01:34:56.810
through the video so the
great 99% of humanity

01:34:56.810 --> 01:34:59.140
who don't understand
science and technology

01:34:59.140 --> 01:35:01.270
can become extremely
appreciative of it

01:35:01.270 --> 01:35:02.459
really almost overnight.

01:35:02.459 --> 01:35:04.000
And that will make
it possible, then,

01:35:04.000 --> 01:35:07.570
to get them oriented towards
exercising the option to make

01:35:07.570 --> 01:35:09.389
it with a design revolution.

01:35:09.389 --> 01:35:10.930
Now coming back to
humans in universe

01:35:10.930 --> 01:35:12.700
and their functioning,
and then the fact

01:35:12.700 --> 01:35:15.750
that they have access to
great design of universe--

01:35:15.750 --> 01:35:17.000
or some of it.

01:35:17.000 --> 01:35:20.080
And they have then also
problems, problems, problems.

01:35:20.080 --> 01:35:22.660
Coming back to that
great big Boeing 747--

01:35:22.660 --> 01:35:25.430
superbly designed, all
those instruments up there,

01:35:25.430 --> 01:35:27.640
giving me all the critical
conditions on board

01:35:27.640 --> 01:35:30.340
the ship, both the power
plant and the airframe--

01:35:30.340 --> 01:35:33.940
I'd say then next to each
one of those instruments

01:35:33.940 --> 01:35:37.300
is liable to be another
dial which would be bringing

01:35:37.300 --> 01:35:40.870
on automated response to the
typical set of conditions

01:35:40.870 --> 01:35:42.390
that I'm obtaining.

01:35:42.390 --> 01:35:45.850
And if those didn't work,
then the pilot himself

01:35:45.850 --> 01:35:48.580
and the engineers could
take over on the controls.

01:35:48.580 --> 01:35:52.330
At any rate, I'd say in order to
have an eternally regenerative

01:35:52.330 --> 01:35:54.000
universe--

01:35:54.000 --> 01:35:57.330
which is what we call a
scenario universe and not

01:35:57.330 --> 01:35:59.671
an instant universe--

01:35:59.671 --> 01:36:01.920
in order to have a totally
regenerative universe which

01:36:01.920 --> 01:36:06.180
is 100% efficient, you'd have
to have some local information

01:36:06.180 --> 01:36:08.580
gathering and some
local problem solving

01:36:08.580 --> 01:36:11.925
in the terms of fundamentals of
design of that universe itself.

01:36:11.925 --> 01:36:14.171
And I say, humans have
been given that capability.

01:36:14.171 --> 01:36:16.170
Quite clearly, we've been
able to go out and get

01:36:16.170 --> 01:36:18.960
that information 11 and 1/2
billion light years around us.

01:36:18.960 --> 01:36:21.180
That we are here for local
information gathering,

01:36:21.180 --> 01:36:25.500
local problem solving in
respect to maintaining

01:36:25.500 --> 01:36:28.419
the integrity of an eternally
regenerative universe.

01:36:28.419 --> 01:36:30.585
Now, nature then, when she
has an important function

01:36:30.585 --> 01:36:34.910
to fulfill, does not
have, as they say,

01:36:34.910 --> 01:36:37.750
all the eggs in one basket.

01:36:37.750 --> 01:36:40.527
She-- for instance, in order
to have humans on the universe

01:36:40.527 --> 01:36:42.110
to do this, we're
going to have to use

01:36:42.110 --> 01:36:43.860
an enormous amount of energy.

01:36:43.860 --> 01:36:46.800
We can't get enough through our
skin from the sun to carry on,

01:36:46.800 --> 01:36:48.710
so we have all the
vegetation impounding

01:36:48.710 --> 01:36:50.430
the sun radiation for us.

01:36:50.430 --> 01:36:52.830
And then we have
that vegetation then

01:36:52.830 --> 01:36:55.050
having to be rooted so
that it can get water,

01:36:55.050 --> 01:36:59.680
it can withstand enormous
winds and also take

01:36:59.680 --> 01:37:02.030
care of its hydraulic
pressure requirements

01:37:02.030 --> 01:37:03.780
and get water back in the sky.

01:37:03.780 --> 01:37:05.700
Because the
vegetation rooted, it

01:37:05.700 --> 01:37:08.370
can't go out and plant its
seeds in preferred places.

01:37:08.370 --> 01:37:10.710
So in nature, then, it
needs this very much

01:37:10.710 --> 01:37:12.970
to keep the human being
going on our planet,

01:37:12.970 --> 01:37:16.320
and she then has each tree
launching little flying

01:37:16.320 --> 01:37:17.760
machines--

01:37:17.760 --> 01:37:21.415
little seeds-- by the
many, many thousands.

01:37:21.415 --> 01:37:25.140
A few of them may land where
they will be prospering.

01:37:25.140 --> 01:37:26.130
Many of them will not.

01:37:26.130 --> 01:37:29.460
So when she has a very important
function and very poor chance

01:37:29.460 --> 01:37:32.430
of survival actually
being realized,

01:37:32.430 --> 01:37:33.550
she makes many starts.

01:37:33.550 --> 01:37:36.570
As I say, she would not have--

01:37:36.570 --> 01:37:39.270
the function we have
to perform would not

01:37:39.270 --> 01:37:42.330
be just in this one little
team on board our little planet

01:37:42.330 --> 01:37:43.470
Earth.

01:37:43.470 --> 01:37:46.060
The same function would
be planted many places

01:37:46.060 --> 01:37:47.070
in the universe.

01:37:47.070 --> 01:37:49.080
In this particularly
one, I say we've now

01:37:49.080 --> 01:37:53.771
come through the being designed
deliberately naked, helpless,

01:37:53.771 --> 01:37:54.270
ignorant.

01:37:54.270 --> 01:37:55.770
We're getting to the
point where we discover

01:37:55.770 --> 01:37:58.230
these beautiful principles,
that our minds are everything,

01:37:58.230 --> 01:38:00.820
that muscle is nothing.

01:38:00.820 --> 01:38:03.870
We're in final examination
now as to whether we're really

01:38:03.870 --> 01:38:05.530
going to qualify.

01:38:05.530 --> 01:38:07.760
And if we'd really qualify,
mind must take over,

01:38:07.760 --> 01:38:09.950
and we must get out
of the way of ever

01:38:09.950 --> 01:38:11.100
having to earn a living.

01:38:11.100 --> 01:38:13.470
That really can't go on
with our real function

01:38:13.470 --> 01:38:16.365
of solving local
problems of the universe

01:38:16.365 --> 01:38:18.990
and getting more and
more information.

01:38:18.990 --> 01:38:21.060
So I think I'll--
our examination from

01:38:21.060 --> 01:38:23.850
my acceleration curve to say
we only have about 10 years

01:38:23.850 --> 01:38:24.480
to make it.

01:38:24.480 --> 01:38:28.306
In fact, I'm down to
about eight years now.

01:38:28.306 --> 01:38:29.430
So it may be shorter still.

01:38:29.430 --> 01:38:30.013
We don't know.

01:38:30.013 --> 01:38:31.680
The acceleration is enormous.

01:38:31.680 --> 01:38:33.480
That's the main thing.

01:38:33.480 --> 01:38:36.510
And so then you say,
what can I do about it?

01:38:36.510 --> 01:38:39.360
The way things are set up now,
all this political system,

01:38:39.360 --> 01:38:42.750
and I don't have anything to do
with the political decisions.

01:38:42.750 --> 01:38:45.206
Everything really depends
on you personally.

01:38:45.206 --> 01:38:46.830
I wish I had a
blackboard here, but I'm

01:38:46.830 --> 01:38:48.960
going to have to do
something with you mentally,

01:38:48.960 --> 01:38:52.590
because we all have
very good imaginations.

01:38:52.590 --> 01:38:55.840
I'm going to give
you a triangle.

01:38:55.840 --> 01:38:59.220
And I'm going to bisect the edge
of that triangle in to connect.

01:38:59.220 --> 01:39:01.709
I've The edge reads two--

01:39:01.709 --> 01:39:02.500
edge module is two.

01:39:02.500 --> 01:39:05.960
There's one, two,
three, four triangles.

01:39:05.960 --> 01:39:09.360
Make a triangle, now the edge
module is going to be three.

01:39:09.360 --> 01:39:15.600
One, two, three four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine.

01:39:15.600 --> 01:39:17.760
Make an edge module of four.

01:39:17.760 --> 01:39:22.540
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine, 10,

01:39:22.540 --> 01:39:25.140
11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16.

01:39:25.140 --> 01:39:29.880
So 16 is two to
the second power,

01:39:29.880 --> 01:39:33.860
and 9 is three to the
second power and so forth.

01:39:33.860 --> 01:39:37.022
You could say triangling
instead of squaring.

01:39:37.022 --> 01:39:39.230
And you find that only a
triangle is the only polygon

01:39:39.230 --> 01:39:40.220
that holds its shape.

01:39:42.950 --> 01:39:48.280
And you discover a
square is two triangles.

01:39:48.280 --> 01:39:51.352
Nature is always
most economical.

01:39:51.352 --> 01:39:52.810
When nature multiplies
herself down

01:39:52.810 --> 01:39:54.680
to the cell, which she
does time and again,

01:39:54.680 --> 01:39:55.640
which is nature doing?

01:39:55.640 --> 01:39:58.830
Triangling or squaring?

01:39:58.830 --> 01:40:00.906
I just gave you
experimental evidence.

01:40:00.906 --> 01:40:02.405
Squares don't even
hold their shape.

01:40:05.010 --> 01:40:08.010
Which is nature using?

01:40:08.010 --> 01:40:11.392
If anybody goes out of
this room saying squaring,

01:40:11.392 --> 01:40:12.350
humanity's all through.

01:40:12.350 --> 01:40:15.492
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:40:15.492 --> 01:40:17.200
FULLER: It's a question
from now on about

01:40:17.200 --> 01:40:20.156
your personal integrity in
daring to really go along

01:40:20.156 --> 01:40:21.280
with experimental evidence.

01:40:21.280 --> 01:40:23.650
And really speak about it,
and do something about it.

01:40:23.650 --> 01:40:25.650
If you do, then the whole
thing's going to work,

01:40:25.650 --> 01:40:27.760
because we do have all
the evidence that we now

01:40:27.760 --> 01:40:29.680
have the capability to make it.

01:40:29.680 --> 01:40:32.590
So it's going to really depend
on your personal integrity.

01:40:32.590 --> 01:40:34.750
I can give you the same
thing showing that--

01:40:34.750 --> 01:40:39.270
I'll make a little cube
out of necklace of tubes.

01:40:39.270 --> 01:40:42.337
It falls down.

01:40:42.337 --> 01:40:44.420
I put triangles together,
it makes the octohedron.

01:40:44.420 --> 01:40:45.180
Holds its shape.

01:40:45.180 --> 01:40:47.170
All triangles do.

01:40:47.170 --> 01:40:51.380
And when we use
a cube for unity,

01:40:51.380 --> 01:40:53.830
as we do in centimeters, grams,
seconds, a cube of water,

01:40:53.830 --> 01:40:56.560
et cetera, et
cetera, et cetera, we

01:40:56.560 --> 01:40:59.840
find that the only reason
it holds the shape it does

01:40:59.840 --> 01:41:04.370
is because you have six square
faces, don't you, on a cube?

01:41:04.370 --> 01:41:08.001
If I put a diagonal
across each face,

01:41:08.001 --> 01:41:10.396
it makes the six edges
of a tetrahedron.

01:41:10.396 --> 01:41:12.020
There's a tetrahedron
holding it there.

01:41:12.020 --> 01:41:16.600
And it has to do that
it has four, one, eight

01:41:16.600 --> 01:41:18.580
octahedron superimposed
on the triangle

01:41:18.580 --> 01:41:20.650
face of the tetrahedron.

01:41:20.650 --> 01:41:22.750
When the tetrahedron is
unity, then the octohedron

01:41:22.750 --> 01:41:24.520
has a volume of
four, and the cube

01:41:24.520 --> 01:41:27.627
is exactly a volume of three.

01:41:27.627 --> 01:41:29.835
And I could go on then to
show you that we can then--

01:41:29.835 --> 01:41:33.130
with the tetrahedon and
octohedron filling space--

01:41:33.130 --> 01:41:35.890
that we can call all
this the third power.

01:41:35.890 --> 01:41:39.357
I can show you quite
clearly the module is one.

01:41:39.357 --> 01:41:40.690
It comes out as one tetrahedron.

01:41:40.690 --> 01:41:44.093
If the edge module is two,
it's eight tetrahedrons.

01:41:44.093 --> 01:41:45.860
If the edge module is--

01:41:45.860 --> 01:41:47.390
remember, tetrahedron
do not fill

01:41:47.390 --> 01:41:48.681
all the space faced by himself.

01:41:48.681 --> 01:41:52.920
They have to be completed by the
octohedron at a volume of four.

01:41:52.920 --> 01:41:59.540
So I can simply show you that
the edge module reads three,

01:41:59.540 --> 01:42:00.790
the volume is 27.

01:42:00.790 --> 01:42:02.790
If the edge module
reads four, the volume

01:42:02.790 --> 01:42:06.341
is 64 of the tetrahedron.

01:42:06.341 --> 01:42:09.220
In terms of-- so I can say
tetrahedroning instead of

01:42:09.220 --> 01:42:10.160
cubing.

01:42:10.160 --> 01:42:11.810
And if I'm using
cubing, I'm using up

01:42:11.810 --> 01:42:13.970
three times as much
universe is available.

01:42:13.970 --> 01:42:16.780
And that's exactly why
the mathematics of science

01:42:16.780 --> 01:42:18.310
is so absolutely ridiculous.

01:42:18.310 --> 01:42:20.530
You had to get an imaginary
number and everything

01:42:20.530 --> 01:42:24.604
to accommodate going
out of this universe.

01:42:24.604 --> 01:42:26.520
Usually tetrahedrons say
right in the universe

01:42:26.520 --> 01:42:29.090
is all conceptual, right
from beginning to end.

01:42:29.090 --> 01:42:33.280
Don't have to have any nonsense
about there are no models.

01:42:33.280 --> 01:42:36.970
When does nature suddenly
check in the models?

01:42:36.970 --> 01:42:39.062
So we say it's
models all the way.

01:42:39.062 --> 01:42:41.020
And all of it is completely
intertransformable.

01:42:41.020 --> 01:42:43.410
But any rate, I go
into it in Synergetics.

01:42:43.410 --> 01:42:46.470
So I say again, if
anybody goes out

01:42:46.470 --> 01:42:50.770
of this room saying cubing when
you see third power, again,

01:42:50.770 --> 01:42:53.750
we're all through, because
you need three times as much

01:42:53.750 --> 01:42:56.390
universe as is available.

01:42:56.390 --> 01:42:57.540
Fairly simple.

01:42:57.540 --> 01:43:00.420
Now, so you--

01:43:00.420 --> 01:43:06.270
I want to really get out what
I feel is what you personally

01:43:06.270 --> 01:43:09.630
can do is going to be
really depending on

01:43:09.630 --> 01:43:14.150
are you willing to really
have everybody accommodated?

01:43:14.150 --> 01:43:17.782
Are you willing to have
everybody really get there?

01:43:17.782 --> 01:43:19.240
Or are you got the
sort of ego that

01:43:19.240 --> 01:43:22.220
doesn't want that to happen,
et cetera, et cetera?

01:43:22.220 --> 01:43:25.880
Are you really going to go along
with the experimental evidence?

01:43:25.880 --> 01:43:27.440
But whether we make
it or not, then,

01:43:27.440 --> 01:43:30.110
is not a matter of how
our leaders behave.

01:43:30.110 --> 01:43:32.690
It's how the humanity
itself behaves.

01:43:32.690 --> 01:43:35.180
It's not a matter of
a few being surviving.

01:43:35.180 --> 01:43:36.800
It's a matter of humanity.

01:43:36.800 --> 01:43:39.260
And humanity's going to go by
virtue of fact you've all now

01:43:39.260 --> 01:43:39.968
got a vocabulary.

01:43:39.968 --> 01:43:42.269
You've all got an enormous
amount of information.

01:43:42.269 --> 01:43:44.060
And then just how much
guts have you really

01:43:44.060 --> 01:43:45.570
got to go along
with information?

01:43:45.570 --> 01:43:49.682
The information is that all
the old systems are obsolete.

01:43:49.682 --> 01:43:51.640
Not because they weren't
good yesterday at all.

01:43:51.640 --> 01:43:54.590
They were absolutely essential,
like the umbilical cord

01:43:54.590 --> 01:43:57.530
was essential at the time
it came out of the womb.

01:43:57.530 --> 01:43:58.924
But we're coming out.

01:43:58.924 --> 01:44:00.840
I'm not saying the flag
wasn't great yesterday

01:44:00.840 --> 01:44:02.510
to what humanity's gone through.

01:44:02.510 --> 01:44:05.570
Incredible courage, and love,
and dedication, humanity

01:44:05.570 --> 01:44:07.550
gets where it is.

01:44:07.550 --> 01:44:10.970
No faults at all with yesterday,
but we're out of that womb.

01:44:10.970 --> 01:44:13.100
We're supposed to
be coming out now,

01:44:13.100 --> 01:44:16.400
and birth is the most
dangerous time of all.

01:44:16.400 --> 01:44:18.280
We're in birth.

01:44:18.280 --> 01:44:21.510
So I am very deeply--

01:44:21.510 --> 01:44:24.155
it's something I haven't said
anything about tonight at all.

01:44:24.155 --> 01:44:27.010
In 1927, I made
up my mind to make

01:44:27.010 --> 01:44:29.782
myself an experimental
experiment to see

01:44:29.782 --> 01:44:31.990
how well the little individual
could really do and do

01:44:31.990 --> 01:44:34.720
everything with artifacts, not
trying to reform human beings,

01:44:34.720 --> 01:44:37.040
but by participating in
the environment itself.

01:44:37.040 --> 01:44:40.090
Because I saw you
and I are 60% water,

01:44:40.090 --> 01:44:41.860
and we're hydraulically
designed--

01:44:41.860 --> 01:44:44.370
hydraulic compression,
et cetera.

01:44:44.370 --> 01:44:47.140
That water freezes and boils,
and all the rest, so we'd

01:44:47.140 --> 01:44:49.290
have to be in the biosphere.

01:44:49.290 --> 01:44:53.940
And any other information
gaining phenomena operating

01:44:53.940 --> 01:44:56.585
on Mars will not look the way
we do on this particular planet

01:44:56.585 --> 01:44:57.940
here in the biosphere.

01:44:57.940 --> 01:45:00.840
So I came to thinking
about many, many things--

01:45:00.840 --> 01:45:04.740
certainly about life,
and integrity, and mind.

01:45:04.740 --> 01:45:07.740
And I came to the
working conclusion--

01:45:07.740 --> 01:45:12.150
I was just overwhelmed by the
a priori intellectual integrity

01:45:12.150 --> 01:45:13.440
of our universe--

01:45:13.440 --> 01:45:15.630
that there were those
generalized principles

01:45:15.630 --> 01:45:20.130
to be discovered, and that they
really were a great design.

01:45:20.130 --> 01:45:23.140
And that it could only be
intellectually expressed

01:45:23.140 --> 01:45:24.450
mathematically.

01:45:24.450 --> 01:45:27.940
So I said, I'm overwhelmed
with a great integrity.

01:45:27.940 --> 01:45:30.510
And I'm assuming
then that I have

01:45:30.510 --> 01:45:33.570
been born at a moment when
somebody's supposed to be

01:45:33.570 --> 01:45:34.760
poking their neck through.

01:45:34.760 --> 01:45:36.180
The information is here.

01:45:36.180 --> 01:45:39.390
And I became really very
much an outsider because--

01:45:39.390 --> 01:45:41.160
I just want you to
understand I did not

01:45:41.160 --> 01:45:43.500
make good at the game of
making money and so forth.

01:45:43.500 --> 01:45:44.880
I lost all of my friends' money.

01:45:44.880 --> 01:45:46.560
I was not only
unknown generally,

01:45:46.560 --> 01:45:49.230
but pretty much a disgrace
to the few who did know me.

01:45:49.230 --> 01:45:51.330
And I said, I'm really
pretty much a throwaway.

01:45:51.330 --> 01:45:53.700
And I'd like to see what
would happen if we really

01:45:53.700 --> 01:45:56.700
made assumptions about all the
things that I'm giving to you.

01:45:56.700 --> 01:45:59.119
That it was implicit
that we could do someday

01:45:59.119 --> 01:46:01.160
so much with so little to
take care of everybody.

01:46:01.160 --> 01:46:03.600
It was also, it
seemed to me, that I

01:46:03.600 --> 01:46:07.360
saw that human beings
having this great hunger

01:46:07.360 --> 01:46:12.184
and so forth, gradually learning
how to domesticate a milk cow,

01:46:12.184 --> 01:46:14.600
then learn how to take the
hide of the cow and make shoes.

01:46:14.600 --> 01:46:16.920
And the shoe man making more
shoes than he could wear.

01:46:16.920 --> 01:46:18.570
And the shoe man
wants a milk cow,

01:46:18.570 --> 01:46:22.530
and the milk cow man cow
wants a pair of shoes.

01:46:22.530 --> 01:46:27.660
They realize they can't cut
the cow up and still milk it.

01:46:27.660 --> 01:46:30.540
So then the man who
grew the milk cow,

01:46:30.540 --> 01:46:32.846
it took him much more time
to grow the milk cow than it

01:46:32.846 --> 01:46:34.200
took a man to make shoes.

01:46:34.200 --> 01:46:36.700
So this is when they invented
money to make up for that.

01:46:36.700 --> 01:46:39.300
So I saw that nature,
then, in order

01:46:39.300 --> 01:46:42.784
to have human life going
on on our planet would

01:46:42.784 --> 01:46:43.950
need a great deal of energy.

01:46:43.950 --> 01:46:46.680
And I spoke about having to
have the vegetation to impound

01:46:46.680 --> 01:46:48.420
the sun radiation for us.

01:46:48.420 --> 01:46:51.270
And incidentally, to be
completely anti-entropic

01:46:51.270 --> 01:46:54.030
as to take the random
seeds and convert them back

01:46:54.030 --> 01:46:56.330
to beautiful, orderly,
molecular structures.

01:46:56.330 --> 01:46:58.460
And which other
creatures could employ

01:46:58.460 --> 01:47:01.890
to grow more and more
orderly types of species

01:47:01.890 --> 01:47:05.070
so that the Earth was a
very anti-entropic affair.

01:47:05.070 --> 01:47:09.210
At any rate, with the vegetation
then doing this impounding

01:47:09.210 --> 01:47:11.850
and being rooted, it couldn't
reach the other vegetation

01:47:11.850 --> 01:47:13.200
to procreate.

01:47:13.200 --> 01:47:16.050
So nature then invented
all the mobile creatures,

01:47:16.050 --> 01:47:19.470
whether worms or butterflies,
to go back and forth

01:47:19.470 --> 01:47:22.530
between all the vegetation
to cross-pollinate them.

01:47:22.530 --> 01:47:24.210
But nature didn't
say to the honey bee,

01:47:24.210 --> 01:47:25.876
I want you to go out
and cross-pollinate

01:47:25.876 --> 01:47:26.760
all this vegetation.

01:47:26.760 --> 01:47:30.650
What nature did was give the
bee a chromosomic instruction

01:47:30.650 --> 01:47:31.692
to go after honey.

01:47:31.692 --> 01:47:33.900
It was continually after
honey, and inadvertently did

01:47:33.900 --> 01:47:35.297
knock off the pollen.

01:47:35.297 --> 01:47:37.380
So I saw nature was
accomplishing all these things

01:47:37.380 --> 01:47:38.460
at 90 degrees.

01:47:38.460 --> 01:47:40.150
You get drive like that.

01:47:40.150 --> 01:47:42.360
So then she had all
the human beings--

01:47:42.360 --> 01:47:43.977
honey money drive--
going after money.

01:47:43.977 --> 01:47:45.060
And they've got a stinger.

01:47:45.060 --> 01:47:48.830
And if anybody tried to take
my money, I'd sting them.

01:47:48.830 --> 01:47:52.950
So I said, what she's really
doing is at 90 degrees.

01:47:52.950 --> 01:47:57.510
So I said, supposing then I
make the working assumption

01:47:57.510 --> 01:47:58.860
that what--

01:47:58.860 --> 01:48:01.050
I've given them to you--
is that we have a function.

01:48:01.050 --> 01:48:02.850
In fact, I've
committed myself to try

01:48:02.850 --> 01:48:05.130
to abet that by developing
environment controls that

01:48:05.130 --> 01:48:08.550
would help to make them able
to function more effectively.

01:48:08.550 --> 01:48:13.000
It could be that if I was doing
what nature wanted, I'd get on.

01:48:13.000 --> 01:48:14.640
It would be very mysterious.

01:48:14.640 --> 01:48:16.290
So I made a working assumption.

01:48:16.290 --> 01:48:17.730
It was enormous.

01:48:17.730 --> 01:48:19.770
I said, I have to
have absolute faith

01:48:19.770 --> 01:48:21.200
in the integrity of universe.

01:48:21.200 --> 01:48:23.100
And that if I'm doing
what nature wants,

01:48:23.100 --> 01:48:24.270
I'll find myself getting on.

01:48:24.270 --> 01:48:27.660
That is 52 years ago, and I
have gone on all this time.

01:48:27.660 --> 01:48:30.690
And I've had to say, only
the impossible has happened

01:48:30.690 --> 01:48:32.879
continually, day after day.

01:48:32.879 --> 01:48:34.170
And I have been able to get on.

01:48:34.170 --> 01:48:36.840
I have been able to get the
artifacts out that I required.

01:48:36.840 --> 01:48:40.650
Really, actually many millions
of dollars, actually-- but I

01:48:40.650 --> 01:48:41.390
never know.

01:48:41.390 --> 01:48:43.345
I have nothing to the
budget, really only up

01:48:43.345 --> 01:48:45.270
to the absolute last second.

01:48:45.270 --> 01:48:48.120
And then if I don't get one, I
realize I'm on the wrong track.

01:48:48.120 --> 01:48:50.571
Because nobody backed
my paper but my own.

01:48:50.571 --> 01:48:52.320
So I had to then say,
let's try this tack.

01:48:52.320 --> 01:48:53.700
That wasn't the tack.

01:48:53.700 --> 01:48:55.869
And what else, what
next needs to be done?

01:48:55.869 --> 01:48:57.660
I've made an incredible
number of mistakes,

01:48:57.660 --> 01:48:58.951
but I've been able to get here.

01:48:58.951 --> 01:49:01.400
But I think it's worth your
while knowing that I do

01:49:01.400 --> 01:49:04.890
represent also an experiment
in seeing if you can get on

01:49:04.890 --> 01:49:07.530
if you really try to do what
nature wants to get done

01:49:07.530 --> 01:49:11.040
rather than how do you
look after yourself.

01:49:11.040 --> 01:49:13.430
Now, that the end.

01:49:13.430 --> 01:49:15.910
I'm overwhelmed by
my faith in this way.

01:49:15.910 --> 01:49:19.090
I tell you that like all human
beings, I couldn't be weaker.

01:49:19.090 --> 01:49:20.200
I've made many mistakes.

01:49:20.200 --> 01:49:23.170
At times, I lose my faith,
and everything goes wrong.

01:49:23.170 --> 01:49:26.630
And every time it gets really
dead, if you yield absolutely,

01:49:26.630 --> 01:49:28.350
then everything just
works out superbly.

01:49:28.350 --> 01:49:34.240
Now-- so I say I know we
have the option to make it.

01:49:34.240 --> 01:49:36.154
I think our time is very short.

01:49:36.154 --> 01:49:37.570
I think if we're
going to make it,

01:49:37.570 --> 01:49:40.325
it's going to be by the
virtue of youth and truth.

01:49:40.325 --> 01:49:41.950
But really the most
extraordinary thing

01:49:41.950 --> 01:49:46.090
about that young world, as all
worlds, is that feeling you had

01:49:46.090 --> 01:49:48.640
of being loved.

01:49:48.640 --> 01:49:51.700
And there's so many feeling
how we're suddenly loving.

01:49:51.700 --> 01:49:55.280
So that young world knows
that stones don't love stones.

01:49:55.280 --> 01:49:57.784
So there's something incredible
in the world of love.

01:49:57.784 --> 01:49:59.950
So I find that young world,
nobody's saying to them,

01:49:59.950 --> 01:50:01.420
get over your
sensitivity anymore.

01:50:01.420 --> 01:50:03.850
They're really are
guarding their sensitivity.

01:50:03.850 --> 01:50:06.460
So they have much more
integrity of daring

01:50:06.460 --> 01:50:08.370
to really go along
with what they see

01:50:08.370 --> 01:50:10.340
and what love tells them.

01:50:10.340 --> 01:50:12.317
So say if we do make
it on a planet--

01:50:12.317 --> 01:50:13.900
I know we have the
option-- it's going

01:50:13.900 --> 01:50:18.450
to be by virtue of the fact
that the youth loves truth.

01:50:18.450 --> 01:50:21.844
And the youth abhors hypocrisy.

01:50:21.844 --> 01:50:25.690
So with the love of truth
of youth, we may make it.

01:50:25.690 --> 01:50:26.680
Thank you.

01:50:26.680 --> 01:50:31.630
AUDIENCE: [APPLAUSE]

01:51:08.176 --> 01:51:09.800
FULLER: I'd have been
very disappointed

01:51:09.800 --> 01:51:12.091
if you didn't do that, and
I stood up hoping you would.

01:51:12.091 --> 01:51:14.410
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHING]

01:51:14.410 --> 01:51:16.750
FULLER: I'm-- for
the last five years,

01:51:16.750 --> 01:51:21.239
I'm averaging an audience
of 1,500 every four days.

01:51:21.239 --> 01:51:23.530
And if you didn't stand up,
you'd be the first audience

01:51:23.530 --> 01:51:23.980
that didn't.

01:51:23.980 --> 01:51:24.813
AUDIENCE: [LAUGHTER]

01:51:24.813 --> 01:51:27.102
FULLER: Now what I feel
is very important for you

01:51:27.102 --> 01:51:27.810
is the following.

01:51:27.810 --> 01:51:30.710
I spoke about 90 degrees
and said it like this.

01:51:30.710 --> 01:51:33.410
It's a free session.

01:51:33.410 --> 01:51:36.449
And if you're in the room
with me and like what I said,

01:51:36.449 --> 01:51:37.740
you say, I liked what you said.

01:51:37.740 --> 01:51:39.323
It reads pretty well
in my experience.

01:51:39.323 --> 01:51:40.770
It seems very reasonable.

01:51:40.770 --> 01:51:43.977
But when you're doing what
you just did, you're saying,

01:51:43.977 --> 01:51:45.560
I'm going to tell
the people beside me

01:51:45.560 --> 01:51:47.000
here that I like what you said.

01:51:47.000 --> 01:51:49.097
So you're talking to
each other and not to me.

01:51:49.097 --> 01:51:50.180
And that's very important.

01:51:50.180 --> 01:51:54.020
Because if we get into very
critical issues ahead here,

01:51:54.020 --> 01:51:55.410
we are very liable to have--

01:51:55.410 --> 01:51:58.760
I want you to remember about
when Germany lost all its money

01:51:58.760 --> 01:52:01.674
in World War I. They got into
a dictatorship, at which point

01:52:01.674 --> 01:52:03.840
nobody is allowed to know
what the other one thinks.

01:52:03.840 --> 01:52:05.600
You're told what to think.

01:52:05.600 --> 01:52:07.270
And we're very
liable-- if we're going

01:52:07.270 --> 01:52:08.790
to come in great
many emergencies,

01:52:08.790 --> 01:52:09.950
there are liable to
be a lot of guns out.

01:52:09.950 --> 01:52:12.499
There are going to be lot of
very sad things may happen.

01:52:12.499 --> 01:52:13.790
But I want you all to remember.

01:52:13.790 --> 01:52:14.810
I'm able to tell you.

01:52:14.810 --> 01:52:17.180
Around the world, I've
been speaking with people.

01:52:17.180 --> 01:52:19.640
People all over respond
as you did just then.

01:52:19.640 --> 01:52:21.720
It's very important for
me be able to tell you

01:52:21.720 --> 01:52:24.200
that apparently I'm
speaking pretty much

01:52:24.200 --> 01:52:25.680
the way humanity
around the world

01:52:25.680 --> 01:52:27.380
would feel it's
reasonable to carry on.

01:52:27.380 --> 01:52:28.050
Thank you.

01:52:28.050 --> 01:52:30.200
AUDIENCE: [APPLAUSE]

